(function () {
  'use strict';
  globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT = Object.assign(globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT || {}, {
    "Carts of coiled rope and sealed lamp-oil wait at the stair-head, requisitioned against the descents of the season.": "一车车盘好的绳索与封存的灯油停在阶梯口，作为本季下行征用的物资。",
    "A recovery party comes up empty at the windlass, and the winch-keeper strikes their number from the slate with a wet thumb.": "搜救队空手回到绞盘旁，绞盘看守用湿拇指从石板上抹去了他们的编号。",
    "Countless tally-marks are scratched into the stone beside the door; none can say what grim account they keep.": "门边的石头上刻满数不清的计数痕，没人说得清它们记着哪一笔凶险的账。",
    "Gold lies drifted to the doorframes like snow, all of it the one dead king's coin, all of it warm.": "金币像积雪一样堆到门框边，尽是同一位亡王的铸币，而且枚枚温热。",
    "The road is paved, cambered and dry, built beyond any craft the Guild commands, and your bootfalls upon it are the only sound for a mile of dark.": "道路铺砌平整，中央隆起且干燥，其工艺远非行会所能掌握；方圆一英里的黑暗中，只听得见你的靴声。",
    "A duergar toll-post stands at the road's shoulder, rates posted in four scripts. The rate for black stone, by weight, has been amended upward three times.": "路肩立着一座灰矮人的收费站，四种文字写着费率。按重量计价的黑石费率已经上调了三次。",
    "Webbing spans the side-galleries in curtains of grey silk, and the bundles hung in it are all facing the road.": "灰色蛛丝如帘幕般横跨两侧长廊，悬在其中的一包包东西全都朝着道路。",
    "A milestone gives the distance to a city whose name has been chiselled off, by order of somebody with excellent tools.": "里程碑标出了通往某座城市的距离；城名奉命被人凿去，下手者用的是极好的工具。",
    "The road holds its camber for miles and sheds the drip to stone gutters at either hand, kept clear and running.": "道路绵延数英里仍保持着拱形坡度，滴水被引入两旁的石沟，沟渠清洁而畅通。",
    "Way-shrines stand at the furlongs, their idols prised out and the niches swept, the offering-cups turned face down.": "每隔一弗隆便立着一座路边神龛，神像已被撬走，壁龛扫得干干净净，供杯也倒扣着。",
    "A freight of covered wagons stands halted at the roadside, the shafts empty, the loads roped down and squared under grey dust.": "一队蒙篷货车停在路边，车辕间空无牲口，货物捆得方方正正，蒙着一层灰尘。",
    "The toll-post's rate-board is amended in a fresh hand, the charge for black stone struck up above every other good it lists.": "收费站的价目板上添了新字迹，黑石收费被改得比板上列出的任何货物都高。",
    "Bootless tracks cross the road in the dust and go on into the dark galleries, spaced to a stride longer than a man's.": "没有穿靴的足迹从尘土中横过道路，一直通向黑暗长廊；步距比人类的步幅更长。",
    "The pieces of the obelisk stand about the field where they fell, each one fenced with votive stakes, and the black stone swallows your lantern-light whole.": "方尖碑的碎块仍立在各自坠落之处，每块周围都围着还愿木桩；黑石将你的灯光吞得一干二净。",
    "The shards hum at the very edge of hearing, all at one pitch, and the pitch rises a shade as you pass between them.": "碎片在听觉边缘发出同一音高的嗡鸣；当你从它们之间经过时，音调又微微升高。",
    "The ground of the field is grown stone, poured and set like candle-wax, and here and there a tool or a boot stands in it to the ankle.": "原野地面是一层生长出来的石头，仿佛烛蜡倾倒后凝固；各处有工具或靴子陷在其中，直没脚踝。",
    "Below the field, under black water, a light moves slowly along the obelisk's root, in the manner of a clerk reading a long document.": "原野下方的黑水中，一点光沿方尖碑根部缓缓移动，仿佛书记员正在逐行阅读一份长文书。",
    "The votive stakes about each shard are hung with tokens and tallies, and the offerings are renewed while the older ones still hang.": "每块碎片周围的还愿木桩都挂着信物与计数牌；旧供物尚未取下，新的又已添上。",
    "The hum of the shards climbs a clear tone as you cross the field's centre, and the fillings of your teeth answer it.": "走过原野中央时，碎片的嗡鸣升成清亮的音调，你牙齿里的填料也随之应和。",
    "A surveyor's sighting-frame stands abandoned on its tripod between two shards, its sights trained true on the obelisk's crown.": "两块碎片之间遗弃着测量员的三脚观测架，瞄具仍准确对着方尖碑顶端。",
    "The poured stone of the ground has set around whatever stood upon it, a boot, a rope-coil, a dropped lamp, and holds them like a fly in amber.": "地面流淌的石质裹住了当时留在上面的一切：一只靴子、一卷绳索、一盏掉落的灯，如同琥珀封住飞虫。",
    "Each shard leans a few degrees off true, and all of them lean the same way, toward the flooded pit at the field's low corner.": "每块碎片都偏离垂直数度，而且全都朝向同一边：原野低处那座被水淹没的坑。",
    "The town below is Mereward to the last cobble, roofed with dark, and the Guildhouse door stands where the Guildhouse door should stand. The head nailed above it is carved of wood.": "地下这座城从头到最后一块石子都与梅里沃德无异，只是头顶覆着黑暗。行会大厅的门也立在它应在的位置，门上钉着的头颅却是木雕。",
    "A bell rings the hour in the counterfeit Guildhouse, seven minutes before the true bell rings it far above.": "赝品行会大厅的钟会提前七分钟报时，随后高处真正的钟声才会响起。",
    "The window of the assay office is painted upon the stone, with a painted clerk behind painted glass, and the painted ledger stands open at today's date.": "化验所的窗口画在石墙上，画出来的玻璃后坐着画出来的书记员，面前摊开的账簿正停在今天的日期。",
    "The lamplighter at the corner has stood upon his ladder through three of your watches, one rung from the top, his taper burning at a fixed length.": "街角的点灯人已经在梯子倒数第二级站过你三轮值守，他手中的点火蜡烛始终燃在同一长度。",
    "The gutters of the false town run with clean water uphill to a cistern, feeding a rain that has never fallen here.": "假城的排水沟里，清水逆坡流向蓄水池，供养着一场从未在此落下的雨。",
    "A market square stands set for a fair, the stalls dressed and the awnings out, every price chalked to the copper on the boards.": "集市广场已经摆好节庆市集，摊位装点妥当，遮篷尽数支起，每块木板上的价格都精确写到一枚铜币。",
    "Your own name is entered on the false Guild roll in the counterfeit hall, in the right hand, on the line above where you signed.": "赝品大厅的假行会名册上也登记着你的名字，笔迹无误，就写在你真正签名位置的上一行。",
    "A dog is fixed mid-stride in the empty street, three legs down and one lifted, its shadow thrown the wrong way from the lamps.": "空街上一条狗凝固在迈步途中，三足着地，一足抬起；灯光却把它的影子投向了错误的方向。",
    "The counterfeit windlass turns at the counterfeit stair-head with no keeper at the crank, paying rope into a shaft with no bottom cut.": "赝品阶梯口的赝品绞盘自行转动，摇柄旁无人看守，绳索不断放进一口没有凿出底部的竖井。",
    "Fresh straw is laid in the empty cages and the feeding troughs stand full: the keeper's rounds are kept to the hour.": "空笼里铺着新鲜稻草，食槽也装得满满当当：看守每个时辰都会准时巡查。",
    "One cage stands closed and chained where the rest are open, its plate scoured blank, its straw pressed flat under a long weight.": "其他笼门都敞开着，唯独一座仍被锁链封住；铭牌已被刮得空白，稻草则被某个长条重物压得平整。",
    "Feathers and cast scales and a shed hide lie swept into tidy heaps at the aisle-ends, gathered and set by for some use.": "羽毛、脱落的鳞片和蜕下的皮被扫成整齐小堆，放在过道尽头，像是收集起来另有用途。",
    "The desks of the scriptorium stand in ranks of forty, and at every desk a pen writes on with no hand to drive it.": "缮写室的书桌四十张一排，桌桌都有一支无人执握的笔仍在书写。",
    "The books upon these shelves are chained to the wood, and a page turns somewhere in the stacks with the patience of a reader in no hurry.": "架上的书全用锁链拴在木板上，书库某处不时翻过一页，耐心如同一位毫不匆忙的读者。",
    "A folio lies open upon a lectern in the aisle: a fair account of your own descent, current to the last stair, in a copyist's hand you have seen upon the Guild ledger.": "过道的斜面书架上摊着一本对开册：它端正记录了你的下行，直到刚走过的阶梯；抄写笔迹你曾在行会账簿上见过。",
    "Ink runs warm in a lead channel along the wall, and the channel is labelled and gated in the manner of a mill-race.": "温热的墨水沿墙边铅槽流淌，槽上既有标签又有闸门，俨然一条磨坊引水渠。",
    "The pens keep one hand across every desk in the hall, the loops and cross-strokes falling together like a rank at drill.": "大厅中每张书桌上的笔都保持着同一种字迹，圆环与横画齐落，如同操练中的队列。",
    "A drying-rail runs the length of the aisle hung with fresh-copied sheets, the topmost still dark and wet at the foot.": "晾纸架贯穿整条过道，上面挂满新抄的纸张，最上方那页底端仍墨色深重、尚未干透。",
    "One desk in forty stands bare of its pen, the inkwell dry and skinned over, the stool drawn back and never set to rights.": "四十张桌中有一张不见笔踪，墨水瓶已经干涸结皮，凳子被拉开后再也没有归位。",
    "The catalogue of the stacks fills a book too heavy for one man to lift, and its own entry is written in on the last page in the same hand.": "书库目录厚重得一人无法抬起，而它自己的条目也以同样的笔迹写在最后一页。",
    "A chained volume lies open at a map of the halls, and a wet line advances upon it stair by stair, keeping your own pace down.": "一本上锁链的书摊开在厅堂地图那页，一条湿润的线正逐阶向前延伸，与你下行的脚步完全同步。",
    "The galleries are hung with mirrors to the roofline, and the lantern comes back a thousandfold, so that you walk at the head of your own procession.": "长廊里的镜子一直挂到屋顶，灯光被千百倍地反射回来，你仿佛走在自己的仪仗队最前方。",
    "One mirror upon the left wall is draped in grey cloth, and the cloth is pinned down at every corner.": "左墙上有一面镜子蒙着灰布，布的每个角都被牢牢钉住。",
    "Your reflection keeps your pace in every glass but one, where it walks a half-step behind and makes the distance up at the turning.": "每面镜中的倒影都与你步调一致，只有一个总落后半步，直到转弯时才赶上。",
    "A signboard in fair lettering asks visitors to leave the mirrors as they found them, by order of the master of the halls. The board is older than the Guild that taught you to read it.": "一块字迹工整的告示牌奉厅堂主人之命，请访客让镜子保持原状。这块牌子比教会你识字的行会还要古老。",
    "The glasses are set at every angle, so the galleries have no end you can walk to, only more galleries folded out of the light.": "镜面以各种角度排列，长廊因此没有可供走到的尽头，只有更多从光线中折叠出来的长廊。",
    "A dust-sheet is drawn over one tall mirror and roped at the corners, and the rope is knotted on the near side, by a hand outside the glass.": "一面高镜罩着防尘布，四角以绳索固定；绳结打在靠外这一侧，出自镜外之手。",
    "Your company of reflections carries lanterns to the roofline at either hand, and every flame among them wavers a beat after your own.": "成群倒影提着灯延伸至两侧屋顶，每一簇镜中火焰都比你的真火慢一拍摇曳。",
    "One pane holds a room you have not entered, furnished and lit, a chair drawn back from a desk as though its clerk had just risen.": "一面镜子映出一间你从未进入的房间，家具齐备、灯火通明；书桌前的椅子被拉开，仿佛书记员刚刚起身。",
    "The frames are gilt and cut alike to the last leaf, save one plain frame of black wood, which gives back none of the light at all.": "所有镜框都镀金雕花，连最后一片叶饰也分毫不差，唯有一面使用朴素黑木框，丝毫不反射光线。",
    "The moulds upon the foundry floor are man-shaped and man-sized, ranked by the hundred, and the nearest score stand open and empty.": "铸造厂地面的模具皆为人形、与真人等大，成百列队；离你最近的二十具敞开着，里面空无一物。",
    "A crucible the size of a cottage hangs cold above the works, and the chains that hold it are dressed and greased to the last link.": "一口小屋般巨大的坩埚冷冷悬在工场上方，承托它的锁链从头到尾都保养上油。",
    "Part-made hands are sorted into bins along the wall by size, palms upward, waiting upon their arms.": "尚未完成的手掌按尺寸分装在墙边箱中，掌心朝上，等待各自的手臂。",
    "The tally-board of the works is chalked in a strong hand: so many poured, so many quickened, and so many returned to the melt for want of obedience.": "工场的计数板上留下有力的粉笔字：浇铸多少，唤醒多少，又有多少因不服从而回炉。",
    "The moulds stand open in ranks down the floor, each the shape of a man laid on his back, the nearest still bright inside from a fresh pour.": "模具成排敞开在地面，每具都像一个仰躺的人；最近那具内部仍因刚刚浇铸而发亮。",
    "Cooling-troughs run black with quenching-oil along the wall, and a film upon one holds the print of a hand that gripped the edge and drew itself out.": "墙边冷却槽里流着漆黑的淬火油，其中一槽的油膜留下一枚手印，像有什么抓住槽边把自己拉了出来。",
    "Finished servitors stand along the far aisle at attention, faceless and numbered on the breast, awaiting the word that sets a rank of them walking.": "完工的仆役在远处过道整齐立正，无面，胸前标着编号，只等一句命令让整排一起迈步。",
    "A gauge-table by the works holds a pattern-hand and a pattern-face in polished brass, against which each casting is checked and passed or broken.": "工场旁的量规台上放着抛光黄铜制成的标准手掌与面孔，每件铸品都要与其比对，再决定合格或砸毁。",
    "The sand of the mould-floor is raked between the rows and printed here and there with bare feet, coming up out of the moulds and leading off toward the stair.": "模具之间的砂地被耙得平整，却零星印着赤足脚印；它们从模具里出来，一路走向阶梯。",
    "The dark overhead is set with lenses after the fashion of stars, and every lens is trained downward upon the halls beneath it.": "头顶的黑暗中嵌着繁星般的镜片，每一片都朝下对准下方厅堂。",
    "Great brass rings turn through the floor and the roof at the pace of a slow clock, and the floor is charted like a heaven, one ring to each floor of the whole descent.": "巨大的黄铜环以慢钟般的速度穿过地板与屋顶旋转，地面绘成星图，每一环对应整段下行中的一层。",
    "A lens the width of a cart-wheel stands over a chart of Mereward, and upon the chart the Guildhouse windlass is drawn in the act of turning.": "一片车轮宽的镜片悬在梅里沃德地图上，图中的行会大厅绞盘正被画在转动的一刻。",
    "Chalk figures ring every chart in the observatory, worked and struck through and worked again, and the newest column of figures is your own tally, entered fair.": "观测台每张图表周围都写满粉笔数字，算过、划掉、再算；最新一列端正记录的正是你的计数。",
    "The great rings carry the whole ceiling of lenses round once in a long watch, and each lens holds one floor of the descent in its glass.": "巨环用一轮漫长值守带着整片镜片穹顶旋转一周，而每片镜中都映着下行的一层。",
    "A lens the size of a millstone stands trained upon the shard-field, and the humming shards show in it ranged like nails in a board.": "一片磨盘大小的镜片对准碎片原野，嗡鸣的碎片在镜中排列如钉入木板的钉子。",
    "Every chart upon the walls is a floor you have crossed, marked with your own road down it in a fresh red line to the stair you took.": "墙上的每张图都是你走过的一层，新鲜红线标出了你的下行路线，一直延伸到你踏上的阶梯。",
    "A brass model of the whole Maw turns in the floor-well, floor beneath floor to the vault, and a single bead descends it a notch as you watch.": "巨口深渊的完整黄铜模型在地井中转动，层层叠至宝库；就在你注视时，一颗独珠又向下降了一格。",
    "The optician's bench holds blanks and half-ground lenses in trays by diameter, and the newest blank is cut to a chart of a hall not yet mapped.": "镜片匠的工作台上，毛坯与磨到一半的镜片按直径分盘摆放；最新的毛坯竟依照一座尚未绘入地图的厅堂切割。",
    "The thrones of the court stand empty in their order of precedence, and the dust upon the arms lies even, as though the sitters rose all at once.": "宫廷王座依尊卑次序空置，扶手上的积尘均匀无扰，仿佛座中人曾在同一刻全部起身。",
    "The mantel above the cold hearth bears a clean ring in the dust where the jar stood through every season you attended.": "冰冷壁炉上方的壁炉架积满灰尘，唯有罐子在你经历的每个赛季里摆放之处留下一圈洁净印记。",
    "The servants' door behind the dais stands open upon a stair going down: the draught from it carries the cold of a room lately left.": "高台后的仆役门敞开着，门后阶梯向下延伸；吹来的风带着一间刚被离开的房间才有的寒意。",
    "The docket of the last season lies upon the clerk's desk, ruled to its final item, and the final item is struck out and not replaced.": "上一赛季的事项表留在书记员桌上，已经填写到最后一项；末项被划掉了，却没有补上新内容。",
    "A row of pegs behind the dais holds the court's liveries, each upon its numbered hook, taken down in order from the highest rank to the lowest.": "高台后的一排挂钩挂着宫廷制服，每件各据编号挂钩，并已从最高阶到最低阶依次取下。",
    "Guttered to their sockets and cold, the great candles of the court have run and set in the shape of the last hour they kept.": "宫廷巨烛已燃至烛台，冰冷凝固，仍保持着最后一次计时时熔流的形状。",
    "The floor before the empty thrones is worn to a shine in the track a clerk walks who carries the same paper to the same chair, season upon season.": "空王座前的地面被磨出一道亮痕，那是书记员逐季把同一份文书送往同一把椅子走出的路线。",
    "You read the ledger open upon the usher's lectern at the head of the room down to the last name entered in it, which is your own, in a hand that waited to enter it.": "你读着厅首司礼员斜面书架上摊开的名册，直到最后登记的名字：正是你自己，出自一只早已等候着写下它的手。",
    "The court's own bell hangs muffled in grey cloth above the dais, tied off so that no hand may ring the season in; the cloth is newly pinned.": "宫廷的钟悬在高台上方，被灰布严密包裹并扎住，任何人都无法鸣钟迎来新赛季；布角才刚钉好。",
    "Every chair of precedence stands pushed back from the table the same distance, just so far as a body pushes a chair to rise.": "所有尊位座椅都从桌边后移了相同距离，恰好是一个人起身时会把椅子推开的幅度。",
    "The Roll above keeps a column for the returned against every name that went below; here, where the returned would be entered, a space is kept clear and waiting.": "上方名册为每个下行者都留有归还一栏；而在这里，本应登记归还者的位置始终空白，静静等待。",
    "Sound does not carry upon the unwritten floor, and your own tread reaches you thin and late, as from a great distance, though you make it underfoot.": "声音无法在未书之层传播；明明脚步就在足下，传回耳中时却微弱迟滞，仿佛来自极远之处。",
    "The floor runs level and featureless past the lantern's reach, and it keeps no landmark, for a landmark is a kind of writing, and this floor takes none.": "平坦无物的地面一直延伸到灯光之外，不留任何地标；地标也是一种书写，而这一层拒绝一切书写。",
    "The dust upon the unwritten floor lies undisturbed, not rising at your passing, settling into no footprint, keeping the floor blank behind you.": "未书之层的灰尘纹丝不动，不因你经过而扬起，也不沉入任何脚印；身后的地面依旧一片空白。",
    "A door stands in the far wall, dressed and hung and never opened, and the wear upon its threshold is all upon the far side, where something waited to be let out and was kept in.": "远墙上立着一扇安装妥当却从未开启的门，门槛磨损全在另一侧；曾有某物在那里等待获释，却始终被关在里面。",
    "The unwritten floor is cold with the cold of a page never written on; it holds the deep in a silence your lantern's small flame does not warm.": "未书之层透着从未落笔之纸的寒意；它用一片连灯中小火也无法温暖的寂静托住深渊。",
    "This deep is the restraint itself: the great chain of it runs through the dark from anchor to anchor, each link the girth of a cart.": "这处深渊本身便是束缚：巨链从一个锚点贯穿黑暗至另一个锚点，每枚链环都有货车般粗大。",
    "The chain lies slack for a mile before you reach the first parted link; the parting is clean, drawn open rather than broken, from the inside of the ring.": "锁链松弛地延伸了一英里，你才见到第一枚分开的链环；断口整洁，不像被击碎，而像从环内被拉开。",
    "Every bond of the chain is signed at its anchor by the warden who set it, the seven signatures in seven hands, the earliest cut deepest into the stone.": "每段锁链的锚点都刻着安设它的守门人签名，七份签名出自七种笔迹，最早那份在石中刻得最深。",
    "The anchors are set into the living rock the girth of a house; from them the chain runs into the dark toward the thing it was set to hold, gone now from the end of it.": "锚具嵌入小屋般粗大的天然岩体，锁链由此伸进黑暗，通向本该被它束缚的东西；如今链端已经空了。",
    "Your torch shows you a single link at a time, and the light does not reach the far side of any of them, and the chain goes on past counting.": "火把一次只能照亮一枚链环，光线甚至够不到链环另一侧；锁链延伸得无从计数。",
    "The parted links lie where they fell open, their cut ends bright and unrusted, drawn wide by a strength that had all the age of the world to spend upon the drawing.": "裂开的链环仍躺在张开时坠落之处，断端明亮无锈；将它们拉开的力量仿佛用尽了世界全部岁月，从容地把缺口越扯越宽。",
    "The first warden's signature is cut at the eldest anchor in the elder script of the Undergate arch, the lead in it untarnished, and the six below it run down to a hand you have come to know.": "第一位守门人的签名以地下门拱上的古老文字刻在最早的锚点，填入其中的铅依旧不见锈蚀；下方六份签名一路延续到一种你已经熟悉的笔迹。",
    "You feel the chain hum a low tone under your hand where it lies slack, cold iron and cart-thick, as a thing lately let go still hums.": "手掌按在松弛的锁链上，能感到货车般粗的冷铁发出低沉嗡鸣，仿佛刚刚松开的东西仍在余振。",
    "A warden's mark is struck into the stone beside each anchor, the seal of the seal it kept, and six of the seven you have seen struck through in lead in the vault above.": "每个锚点旁的石上都打着守门人印记，是守护封印者自己的封印；七枚中有六枚，你已在上方宝库见过以铅划销。",
    "Older than the dark of any floor above it, the dark of this deep carries the chain through toward the waking ground, where the last of it lies parted and slack.": "这里的黑暗比上方任何楼层都古老，锁链穿行其中，通往苏醒之地；在那里，最后一段锁链裂开而松垂。",
    "Where the chain is whole it holds its line true across the deep, and where it is parted the two ends lie a mile apart, drawn open at leisure by what they held.": "锁链完整之处笔直横贯深渊，断裂之处两端却相隔一英里，像是被它曾束缚的东西不紧不慢地拉开。",
    "Every omen of the descent comes home upon the waking ground: the flood that ebbed and returned in the drowned undertemple as though the temple breathed, the tread you felt through the floor of the halls, and the counting.": "下行途中的每个预兆都在苏醒之地找到了源头：溺没地下神殿里如呼吸般涨退的洪水，厅堂地板下传来的脚步，还有那持续不断的计数。",
    "Tally-marks are cut into the bedrock here in a hand too large to read up close, grouped in sevens; the newest mark is bright, cut since the Last Vault fell silent above you.": "此处基岩上刻着七个一组的计数痕，字迹巨大，近看反而无法辨读；最新一痕仍然明亮，是在上方最终宝库归于沉寂后才刻下的。",
    "The ground breathes: it lifts under your boots the width of a hair and settles, slow as a sleeper, and the ebb and return of it is the rhythm the drowned undertemple kept.": "地面正在呼吸：它在靴下抬起一丝发宽，又缓缓落定，如同沉睡者；这一涨一落正是溺没地下神殿一直保持的节奏。",
    "The tread you felt through the floor of the manor halls is the ground's own: here you stand upon the thing that made it, stirring beneath you as you cross.": "你在庄园厅堂地板下感到的脚步，原来属于这片地面本身；如今你正站在制造那动静的东西上面，它在你走过时于足下翻动。",
    "The tally-marks run across the bedrock in courses, seven and seven and seven, cut so large that you must stand off a hundred paces to read a single seven whole.": "计数痕一行行横贯基岩，七个又七个，再七个；每组都大得惊人，必须退开百步才能看全一个“七”。",
    "A single mark stands bright and fresh at the end of the newest seven, cut into the old stone since the drum above fell silent, and its edges are not yet worn.": "最新一组七痕末尾，有一道刻痕明亮崭新；它是在上方鼓声停息后才刻入古石，边缘尚未磨损。",
    "As you cross the waking ground the heat climbs, the stone of it warm against your palm, warmer than the seal ever wept, the warmth rising from below.": "走过苏醒之地时，热度不断升高；石头贴着掌心已经温热，比封印渗出的水更暖，而热意来自下方。",
    "The counting you have heard in tally-marks and drums and sevens since the goblin warren is written here at its full size, in the hand of the thing that has kept it.": "自哥布林巢穴以来，你从刻痕、鼓声与一个个“七”中听见的计数，如今以完整尺寸写在这里，出自那一直维持计数之物的手。",
    "The ground stirs and the dust rises from the tally-marks in a thin grey breath and settles back into the cuts, and the marks stand clear again, and the count is kept.": "地面翻动，灰尘从计数痕中如一口灰气般升起，又落回凹槽；刻痕重新清晰，计数仍在继续。",
    "Far below the waking ground a glow shows through the seams of the stone, faint and golden and even; it brightens and dims with the breathing of the ground.": "苏醒之地的遥远下方，一层微弱、金黄而均匀的光从石缝透出，随地面的呼吸明灭。",
    "The waking ground is the last floor with a name; past its edge the stone falls away toward the Bottom, the glow coming up out of the fall to meet you.": "苏醒之地是最后一个拥有名字的楼层；越过边缘，岩石便向最底层坠落，光芒从深处升起迎接你。",
    "This is the first hoard, older than Malgrith's by an age, and the coin of it is struck with the faces of kings the Roll gives no seasons to and the Guild's books never named.": "这是最初的宝藏，比马尔格里斯的宝库还古老一个时代；金币上铸着历代国王的面孔，名册未曾记录他们的赛季，行会书册也从未提及其名。",
    "The glow you took for gold this far down is the light of the thing breathing; it comes up through the coin from below and brightens as you climb down toward it.": "一路深入时你以为属于黄金的光泽，其实来自那个正在呼吸的东西；光从金币下方透上来，随着你朝它下行而愈发明亮。",
    "Warm underfoot, all of it, warm as a hand, the coin shifts and rings beneath your boots with the slow breathing of what lies beneath it.": "脚下所有金币都像手掌一样温热，随着下方存在的缓慢呼吸，在靴底移动、叮当作响。",
    "The hoard runs down and down toward the glow, coin upon coin without a floor to it, struck by a hundred kingdoms the surface has forgotten and the deep has kept.": "宝藏层层向光芒深处倾落，金币叠着金币，下面不见地面；它们来自百个已被地表遗忘、却被深渊保存的王国。",
    "The coin lies face-up, every piece, the same faces from a hundred mints, and the faces are warm, and the metal of them holds the heat of the breathing below.": "每枚金币都正面朝上，百家铸币厂打出的却是同一批面孔；面孔温热，金属中存着下方呼吸传来的热量。",
    "The walls of the Bottom are scored the way the Wyrm's vault was scored, by something that left this place once, an age ago; the stone keeps no mark of any arrival, for it was always here.": "最底层墙壁上的划痕与巨龙宝库如出一辙，是某个东西在久远年代离开此地时留下的；石上没有任何抵达痕迹，因为它本来就一直在这里。",
    "The glow is even and golden and comes from no lamp: it dims and brightens the slow breadth of a long breath, the coin dimming and brightening with it.": "均匀的金光并非来自任何灯火；它随着一口漫长呼吸缓慢明灭，金币也一同黯淡、亮起。",
    "You took this glow for the gold of a hoard once before, in the Wyrm's Vault where Malgrith slept, and here at last it is the thing itself, breathing in its bed of coin.": "你曾在马尔格里斯沉睡的巨龙宝库里，把同样的光误认作黄金反光；而在这里，你终于见到光源本身，正躺在金币床上呼吸。",
    "As you climb down the heat climbs until, by the last of the descent, the coin is hot to the hand; the air moves with a slow tide, in and then out, that is not the wind.": "越往下走，热度越高；抵达下行末端时，金币已烫手。空气像缓慢潮汐般一进一出，却不是风。",
    "The first hoard was laid down to bury the debt beneath it, coin upon coin an age deep, and the debt has kept warm under it, counting, and the count is nearly told.": "最初的宝藏被堆来掩埋下方的债务，金币层层叠了一个时代之深；债务一直在下面保持温热、默默计数，而数字即将数完。",
    "At the foot of the hoard the coin gives way to the glow, the glow to the thing that makes it: the whole descent has been a fall toward this floor.": "在宝藏底部，金币让位于光芒，光芒又让位于制造它的东西；整段下行，原来都是朝这一层坠落。",
    "The moor runs flat and brown to every horizon, and the road across it is a Guild road for four miles and a cart-track for the rest.": "荒原平坦褐黄，向每一处地平线延伸；横穿其上的道路只有前四英里属于行会，余下不过是车辙。",
    "The last waystone bears the Guild's chalk and the Guild's arrow, and beyond it the chalk stops, for no surveyor has been paid to go further.": "最后一块路标石上留着行会粉笔与行会箭头；再往前便没有粉笔记号，因为没人付钱让测量员走得更远。",
    "A standing bank of mist lies across the road ahead, grey as wet wool, and it has lain there in the same place since before the Guild kept records of the moor.": "前方一道灰如湿羊毛的雾墙横卧路上；早在行会开始记录这片荒原之前，它便一直停在同一位置。",
    "Sheep-bones lie bleached in the heather beside the track, picked clean and lying where they fell, with no shepherd within a day's walk to account for them.": "车辙旁的石南丛中散着晒白的羊骨，被啃得干干净净，仍保持倒毙时的位置；方圆一天脚程内都找不到牧羊人解释它们的来历。",
    "The wind comes off the moor with rain in it, and the gorse rattles, and the mist ahead moves not at all for any wind that blows.": "风裹着雨意掠过荒原，金雀花沙沙作响；无论风怎样吹，前方迷雾都纹丝不动。",
    "A carrier's cart stands abandoned at the roadside with its shafts down and its load still roped, and the harness has been cut through rather than unbuckled.": "一辆货运马车被遗弃在路边，车辕垂地，货物仍捆在车上；挽具不是解开的，而是直接割断。",
    "You pass a wayside cross with its arms broken off and its inscription cut away, and the cut is old and deliberate and made with a good chisel.": "你经过一座路边十字架，横臂被折断，铭文被凿去；凿痕古老、刻意，而且使用了上好的凿子。",
    "The birds of the moor turn back at a fixed line in the air, all of them, as though the sky above the mist were a wall they have long since learned.": "荒原上所有飞鸟都会在空中同一条界线前折返，仿佛迷雾上方的天空是一堵它们早已熟知的墙。",
    "The mist closed behind you upon the road and stands there yet, and the way back out of the Vale is the way you came, and the way you came is gone.": "迷雾在你身后的路上合拢，至今仍立在那里；离开山谷只能原路返回，而来路已经消失。",
    "Every shutter in Hollowmere is barred upon the street side, and the bars are new oak, and they were fitted by the village to the village.": "空心湖村每扇百叶窗都从临街一侧上了闩，门闩是新橡木，装设者与防范对象都是这个村庄本身。",
    "The crag stands over the whole valley with the castle upon it, and there is no hour of the day when the castle is not in sight of the street.": "峭壁高踞整座山谷，城堡立于其上；一天中的任何时辰，从街上都能看见它。",
    "A tally is cut into the doorpost of the Bell and Shutter, one notch a night, and the notches run the length of the post and begin again at the top.": "“钟与百叶窗”旅店的门柱上刻着计数，每夜一道；刻痕排满整根门柱后，又从顶端重新开始。",
    "The villagers speak to you civilly and at length and about the weather, and every one of them stands so that the crag is at their back.": "村民礼貌而冗长地与你谈论天气，每个人说话时都让峭壁位于自己背后。",
    "Bread is set out upon three doorsteps in the evening, wrapped in cloth and left, and it is gone by morning, and no one in Hollowmere will say who takes it.": "傍晚时，三户人家的门阶上会留下布包面包；天亮前面包便消失，而空心湖村无人肯说是谁取走了它。",
    "The well in the square is boarded over and nailed, and the village draws its water from the beck instead, and carries it further for the privilege.": "广场水井被木板封死并钉牢，村民改从溪流取水，为此甘愿多走一段路。",
    "At dusk the whole street goes indoors at once, without a bell to call them, and the barring of the shutters runs down the row like a roll of drums.": "黄昏一到，整条街的人无需钟声召唤便同时进屋；百叶窗依次落闩，声音沿街传去，如一阵鼓点。",
    "The Thornwake drowned when the mill-race was cut, and its trees stand dead in standing water with the bark gone off them and the heartwood grey.": "磨坊引水渠开凿时，刺棘林被淹没；树木死立在积水中，树皮尽脱，心材灰白。",
    "Thorn has taken the whole wood since the drowning, black thorn a foot thick, grown through and over every fallen trunk in a mat no axe will open.": "被淹之后，荆棘占据了整片树林；一英尺粗的黑刺穿过、盖住每根倒木，织成连斧头也劈不开的密网。",
    "The water between the trees is dark and knee-deep and holds no fish, and it carries the smell of iron rather than the smell of a marsh.": "树间积水漆黑及膝，不见一尾鱼；水里带的是铁味，而不是沼泽气息。",
    "Deer-paths run through the thorn in every direction, cut clean at the height of a man's shoulder, and no deer has been seen in this Vale for an age.": "鹿径从各个方向穿过荆棘，在人类肩高处被整齐削开；然而这座山谷已有一个时代没人见过鹿。",
    "Something has been hung in the branches at intervals along the drowned ride, wrapped and roped and swinging, and it is set too high for any hand to have reached.": "被淹没的林间道沿途，每隔一段便有某样东西裹好、捆紧，吊在枝头摇摆；悬挂位置高得绝非人手能够触及。",
    "Down the servants' stair the smell of the court thins away and the smell of old paper rises to meet you, dry and close, from the offices below.": "沿仆役阶梯下行，宫廷的气味渐渐淡去，地下办公室里干燥而贴近的旧纸气息迎面升起。",
    "Every warden's name is entered at the head of a season in a firm hand, and struck through at the foot of it in a fainter one.": "每位守门人的名字都以有力笔迹写在赛季开头，又以更浅的笔迹在赛季末尾划去。",
    "The earliest volumes of the Roll are written in the elder script of the Undergate arch, and the lead of their bindings is untarnished.": "名册最早的卷册以地下门拱上的古文字写成，书脊中的铅封至今未染锈色。",
    "The stacks of the Roll run back into the dark past the lantern's reach, shelf above shelf: every shelf is dated at its end in a clerk's small hand.": "名册书架一层叠一层，向灯光照不到的黑暗深处延伸；每层末端都用书记员细小的笔迹标着日期。",
    "You pass a reading-desk at each bay, a volume chained open upon it, the chain worn bright where a reader's hand has drawn the book to the light.": "每个书架间隔都有一张阅读桌，桌上摊着用链条锁住的卷册；读者把书拖向灯光之处，链条在那里磨得发亮。",
    "The manifest of the sealed is kept in double column, the name upon the left and the term served upon the right; the right-hand column of the eldest volumes runs to figures no season could hold.": "封印名录分左右两栏，左栏写姓名，右栏写服役期限；最古老卷册的右栏记录着任何赛季都容纳不下的数字。",
    "The ink of the striking-through is a paler ink than the enrolling, mixed thinner, as though the hand that struck each name had less to spend upon the closing than upon the opening.": "划销姓名的墨色比登记时更浅，调得也更稀，仿佛划掉名字的手在终结时能用的墨比开头更少。",
    "A ladder upon rails stands against the highest stacks, and the rungs are worn only at the top, where a climber reaches always for the same high shelf.": "一架带轨梯子靠在最高书架旁，只有顶端横档磨损严重；攀爬者总是伸手去取同一层高架上的书。",
    "The volumes are shelved by season without a gap, save one bay left standing empty at the near end, swept and dated ahead, waiting upon a volume not yet bound.": "卷册按赛季连续排放，唯有近端留着一个空格，已清扫并预先标好日期，等待一本尚未装订的卷册。",
    "Fallen in an aisle, a lead binding lies open where it dropped, its pages spilled and every name upon them struck through in the same hand.": "过道里掉落着一本打开的铅封书，书页散落，页上每个名字都被同一只手划去。",
    "The dust upon the reading-desks is disturbed in a single track down the centre of the hall, the track of a reader who visits every bay in turn and lingers at none.": "阅读桌上的灰尘只在大厅中央留下一条扰动的路径，像某位读者逐一走过每个间隔，却从不在任何处停留。",
    "At the hall's far end a fresh volume stands part-bound in the vice, its lead covers cut and its pages blank, and the enrolling-pen lies across it, charged with ink.": "大厅尽头，一本新卷册夹在台钳中，铅封书皮刚裁好，内页仍是空白；登记笔横放其上，墨水饱满。",
    "Seven tombs stand in the gallery, each cut in the fashion of its age, and the silver flood-mark upon the third names the Drowned Celebrant as its tenant.": "长廊里立着七座墓，每座都按所属时代的样式凿成；第三座上的银色水痕写着“溺亡祭司”之名。",
    "An eighth tomb is begun in the far wall, the outline chalked and the first course cut, and the chalk gives no name.": "远墙上正在开凿第八座墓，轮廓已用粉笔画出，第一层石块也已切开，但粉笔没有写下名字。",
    "Newest cut and sharpest of them all, the sixth tomb wears an effigy in a mage's cuffs turned back for the work, in the fashion of the halls above.": "第六座墓是最新、棱角最利的一座，墓上雕着身穿卷袖法师长袍的肖像，样式仿照上方厅堂。",
    "Every effigy is carved with its hands crossed upon the seal it kept, the seven seals all different, each cut true to its impression.": "每尊肖像都双手交叠压在自己守护的封印上；七枚封印各不相同，每道雕痕都精准复刻其印记。",
    "The obelisk of the shard-field was riven into seven, one piece to each warden's seal, and the sevens the goblins learned to count in the deep were the count of the seven kept here, so that shard and seal and warden are one tally told three ways.": "碎片原野的方尖碑被劈成七块，各对应一位守门人的封印；哥布林在深处学会的“七”正是这里保存的七数，因此碎片、封印与守门人其实是同一笔计数的三种说法。",
    "The eighth tomb's chalked outline is cut to a figure of a living height and reach, the mason's cord and plumb hanging lately used from a nail beside it.": "第八座墓的粉笔轮廓按活人的身高与臂展凿刻，石匠用过的墨线与铅锤仍挂在旁边的钉子上。",
    "At the gallery's head a bench of offerings stands, the offerings numbered tags of the Guild's own issue, laid down in rows and gathering dust.": "长廊尽头立着一张供奉台，供物都系着行会发放的编号牌，整齐排放，渐渐覆上灰尘。",
    "The far wall past the eighth tomb is dressed and squared for a ninth tomb and a tenth: the gallery is cut deeper than its tenants, in the manner of a room that expects to fill.": "第八座墓之后的远墙已经修整方正，预备开凿第九与第十座；长廊挖得比现有墓穴更深，像一间等着继续填满的房间。",
    "A great chain runs the gallery from staple to staple, gathered at each cell door into a lock, and every lock is filed through from the inside.": "一条巨链从一个锚钉延伸到另一个，经过每扇牢门时收进锁中；每把锁都从内部被锉穿。",
    "The terms of each debt are posted upon the cell door in a fair hand: the figures run to sums no debtor could serve in the years of a life, nor of ten.": "每扇牢门上都用端正字迹写着债务条款；数字高到任何债务人一生、甚至十生都无法偿还。",
    "The seal is thinnest in this deep; the wet of it stands upon the walls in a cold sweat, gathers in the gutters of the floor, then runs downward.": "封印在此深处最为薄弱；湿气像冷汗凝在墙上，汇入地面沟槽，再向下流去。",
    "You find the cells standing open upon their filed locks, the straw within each pressed flat in the one corner where a tenant sat a long age against the wall.": "你发现牢门都敞开着，锉穿的锁还挂在门上；每间牢房的稻草都在靠墙一角被压平，仿佛囚徒在那里坐了漫长岁月。",
    "A tally is scratched beside each door in the tenant's own hand, counting the seasons in sevens, and the counting on the deepest doors runs off the stone and onto the frame.": "每扇门旁都由囚徒亲手刻着计数，以七为一组记录赛季；最深处门旁的数字甚至越过石墙，刻到了门框上。",
    "The chain is cold iron, cart-thick, scored bright at every lock where a file has worked it patiently through from within the cell.": "锁链是冰冷的铁，粗如车轴；每把锁旁都留着明亮锉痕，显然有人从牢内耐心地锉穿它。",
    "The gutters of the gallery carry the seal's weeping downward toward a grating; the grating is choked with the grey silt of an age of the water passing.": "长廊沟槽承接封印渗出的水，向下流至栅格；栅格被历经一个时代的灰色水淤堵塞。",
    "A debtor's writ is nailed above one door, drawn in the court's own form, and the named party upon it is struck out and the sum carried forward to the door below.": "一扇门上方钉着债务人的传票，格式是宫廷专用样式；传票上姓名已被划去，债额则转记到下方那扇门。",
    "The air of the deep is colder than the floors above it and moves upward past you, drawn toward the empty court as a draught is drawn toward an open flue.": "深处空气比上方楼层更冷，正从你身边向上流动，朝空置宫廷而去，如同烟气被敞开的烟道吸走。",
    "Broken outward, the deepest cells have had their doors carried off the hinges from within, the marks upon them the marks of a shoulder set against them and heaved.": "最深处牢房的门向外破开，整扇门从内部被掀离铰链；门上的痕迹显示曾有人用肩膀抵住它猛推。",
    "A ledger of the indebted lies chained to the warder's desk at the gallery-head, and the accounts within it are ruled forward season upon season and closed not once.": "债务账簿用链条锁在长廊尽头的看守桌上，账目一季接一季向后登记，却从未结清过一次。",
    "The drum you have heard since the goblin warren beats here: a counterweight upon a beam, keeping the count of the works in sevens.": "自哥布林巢穴以来你听见的鼓声就在这里敲响：横梁上的配重以七为组，记录工场的运转。",
    "The seal weeps, and the works return the weeping to the wound; the water you have waded upon every floor above begins in this room.": "封印不断渗水，工场又把渗水送回伤口；你在上方每一层涉过的水，都始于这个房间。",
    "The beam of the works is a single timber the length of a gallery, hung upon a pivot of dressed stone; it rises and falls to the drum's own slow count.": "工场横梁由一根长及整条长廊的木材制成，悬在修整过的石轴上，随着鼓声缓慢计数而起落。",
    "You pass pumps the height of a house down the wall of the works, drawing the gathered water up and driving it back against the seal, labouring and taking no rest.": "工场墙边排列着小屋般高的水泵，它们抽起汇集的水，再压回封印，劳作不息。",
    "The counterweight is a block of the black stone, cut square and hung in chains, swinging its short arc between two worn hollows, one at either end of the beat.": "配重是一块切成方形、以锁链悬挂的黑石，在两个磨损凹槽之间短幅摆动，鼓点两端各有一处。",
    "Gauges of brass and bone stand ranked upon the works' face: every needle upon them holds at its mark, watched by no hand and corrected by no hand.": "黄铜与骨制仪表在工场正面排列整齐；所有指针都停在刻度上，无人监看，也无人校正。",
    "The floor of the works is cut in channels that gather the seal's weeping from every side: they run to the pumps in a fall so slight the water seems to climb.": "工场地面凿有沟渠，从四面收集封印渗水；沟渠坡度小得几乎不可察，水看起来反而像在向上流。",
    "Dressed and greased to the last link, the chains of the works carry a fresh grease, laid on by a hand that keeps the machinery though the court above it stands empty.": "工场锁链连最后一环都修整上油，油脂仍然新鲜；即便上方宫廷已经空置，仍有一只手维护着这套机械。",
    "A maintenance-book hangs upon a nail by the beam, its columns ticked to the present hour, and the hand that ticks them counts the strokes of the drum and enters them in sevens.": "横梁旁钉子上挂着维护簿，各栏勾记到当前时辰；负责打勾的手数着鼓点，并以七为组登记。",
    "The whole room labours upon one purpose plainly read: to gather the water the seal lets weep, to drive it back against the wound, and to keep the count while it drives.": "整座房间只为一个显而易见的目的运转：收集封印渗出的水，将其压回伤口，并在压送时持续计数。",
    "Far below the works the beam's fall is answered, a beat late, by a deeper sound that is not the drum, and the needles upon the gauges lean the merest hair at the answering.": "工场遥远下方，有一道并非鼓声的低沉响动，总在横梁落下后慢一拍回应；回应响起时，仪表指针会轻微偏转。",
    "The Last Vault is furnished as a study and kept as a fortress, and the jar stands upon the mantel, dusted and centred, with the fire laid ready beneath it.": "最终宝库按书房布置，却像堡垒般守备；罐子除去灰尘，端正放在壁炉架中央，下方炉火已经备好。",
    "The vault is walled in the black stone to a thickness no ram could tell; the one door is the servants' door at your back, which carries no bar upon this side.": "宝库以黑石砌墙，厚得任何攻城槌都无法探明；唯一入口是你身后的仆役门，而门的这一侧没有门闩。",
    "A great desk stands at the vault's heart, ordered and clean, the enrolling-pen laid square upon a blank first page of a new Roll, the ink charged.": "宝库中央立着一张整洁有序的大书桌，登记笔端正放在新名册空白的第一页上，笔尖已饱蘸墨水。",
    "The fire beneath the jar is laid and not lit, the kindling set and the tinder dry, in the manner of a hearth kept ready against an hour that has not yet come.": "罐子下方的炉火已经架好却未点燃，细柴就位，引火物干燥，仿佛壁炉正为尚未到来的时刻随时待命。",
    "The shelves of the study run to the vault-roof with the working-books of an age, ordered by hand and by season: every one is a warden's own account of the keeping.": "书房架子直抵宝库屋顶，摆满一个时代的法术书，按笔迹与赛季分类；每一本都是守门人亲手写下的守护记录。",
    "You see the jar upon the mantel, plain clay, stoppered and sealed with lead, the dust wiped from it in a clean ring though it lies thick upon all else.": "壁炉架上的罐子只是普通陶罐，塞住瓶口并以铅封缄；别处积尘厚重，唯独罐子周围被擦出一圈干净痕迹。",
    "A single chair stands to the desk, worn to its sitter through a long age of sitting, and the account open upon the desk is ruled to the present season and no further.": "书桌旁只有一把椅子，漫长岁月的端坐已将它磨出主人身形；桌上摊开的记录只写到当前赛季，不再向后。",
    "Trimmed to last, the lamps of the vault burn steady and low, the oil-jars ranked beneath them holding enough to keep the light through an age of nights.": "宝库灯芯经过修剪，火焰低而稳定；下方成排油罐足以让灯光燃过一个时代的黑夜。",
    "Upon the wall behind the desk hang the seven seals of the wardens in their order, six of them struck through in lead, and the seventh whole and waiting.": "书桌后方墙上依次挂着七位守门人的封印，其中六枚已用铅划销，第七枚仍然完整，静候其时。",
    "The vault is warm where the deeps above it are cold; the warmth rises through the floor from below, in the manner of a hearth banked in the room beneath.": "上方深处寒冷，这座宝库却很温暖；热意从地板下升起，仿佛楼下房间的壁炉仍压着余火。",
    "The count is kept plainly here in a firm old hand: every warden entered, every warden struck, and a place ruled clean at the foot of the page for the name that keeps the count next.": "此处以苍劲旧笔清楚维持着计数：每位守门人都曾登记、又被划销，页脚还整洁留出一格，等待下一位维持计数者的名字。",
    "The last door stands open at your back: no warden of the seven ever crossed its sill and lived to be entered as returned.": "最后一扇门在你身后敞开；七位守门人中，从未有人跨过这道门槛后活着回来接受登记。",
    "The water that rose against the whole descent runs the other way here, over the sill and down into the dark, unhurried.": "一路逆着整段下行上涨的水，在这里转向另一边，不紧不慢地越过门槛，流入黑暗。",
    "The wards upon the door are cut clean through; the tool-marks are the same the assay office would give a year's budget to read, off the Undergate arch far above.": "门上的防护符文被整齐切穿，工具痕迹与遥远上方地下门拱上的相同；化验所曾愿花整年预算研究那种痕迹。",
    "The threshold is worn in one direction only, by the long file of feet that went down; the far edge of the sill keeps its mason's arris still.": "门槛只朝一个方向磨损，是漫长队列向下走过所致；槛石远侧仍保留石匠凿出的锐利棱线。",
    "The great lock of the door hangs open upon its hasp, its wards cut through rather than forced, by a hand with better tools than the Guild has ever owned.": "门上巨锁敞开挂在锁扣上，锁簧不是被蛮力破坏，而是被利器切穿；下手者拥有行会从未见过的精良工具。",
    "Cold air pours over the sill and down with the water, drawn to the deep below as the whole Maw has been drawn, floor upon floor, since the first stair.": "冷空气随流水越过门槛倾泻而下，被下方深处吸引；从第一段阶梯起，整座巨口深渊便这样一层层被引向它。",
    "Something vast was dragged across the stone of the threshold once, going down, scoring it an age before the first warden was set to keep it.": "曾有某个庞然大物被拖过门槛石向下而去；早在第一位守门人受命看守前一个时代，它就留下了这道划痕。",
    "A warden's post stands at the sill, a lectern and a stool and a lamp long cold, kept facing the door from the inside, for the watch was always kept against what lay below.": "门槛旁设着守门人岗哨，斜面书架、凳子和早已冰冷的灯都从内侧面向大门，因为警戒对象始终是下方之物。",
    "You watch the water fall over the sill in a smooth unbroken sheet that makes no sound at the foot of it, for the foot of it is too far down to hear.": "你看着水流以平滑不绝的水幕越过门槛，落处没有声音，因为它落得太深，已经无法听见。",
    "The marks of the Grey Procurer's tools are upon every ward and hinge, the silent roads' own work, filling an order placed by the thing at the bottom an age ago.": "每道符文与每只铰链上都有灰色采办官的工具痕迹，这是寂静道路的工艺，履行着最底层之物在一个时代前下达的订单。",
    "Beyond the sill the stair goes down into a dark your torch does not lighten; the cold of it is the cold of deep water, rising to meet you.": "门槛之外，阶梯向火把也无法照亮的黑暗下降；深水般的寒意从中升起迎接你。",
    "This is the oldest stratum of the Maw, and it was worked from the far side: every chisel-stroke in the stone rises toward the surface, cut by a hand standing below and reaching up.": "这是巨口深渊最古老的地层，而且由另一侧开凿；石上的每道凿痕都朝地表上升，出自站在下方、向上伸手的工匠。",
    "The galleries are ceilinged like roofs, their floors open to the deep below, built to be looked at from beneath by what raised them.": "长廊顶面如屋顶般修饰，地面却向下方深渊敞开；建造它们的东西原本要从下方向上观赏。",
    "The water stands deep and still in the foundation; the drowned stonework beneath it is dressed as fair as any mason's above, older than masons.": "地基里的水深而静，水下石工与上方任何石匠的作品一样精美，却比石匠这个行当更加古老。",
    "The Maw was dug from both ends, and here the two diggings meet: the wardens' stair coming down from above, and this, rising to meet it from the deep.": "巨口深渊从两端同时开凿，两条工程在此相遇：守门人阶梯从上方下降，而这一段从深处向上迎来。",
    "A founder's mark is cut into a keystone at the waterline, in no script the survey carries, and it is cut upside down to a reader coming from above.": "水线处拱顶石刻着建造者标记，不属于勘测队记录的任何文字；对从上方而来的读者来说，它是倒置的。",
    "The tool-marks in the drowned stone are the length of a man's forearm, climbing the walls in even courses, the work of a patient hand and a long age.": "淹没石块上的工具痕迹长及人类前臂，均匀分层向墙上攀升，是耐心工匠耗费漫长时代的作品。",
    "Pillars rise from the black water in ranks, dressed and fluted: they carry a roof that was meant to be a floor for a country the sun never reached.": "修整过并带凹槽的石柱成排从黑水升起，托着一片本应作为地面的屋顶，属于一个阳光从未照到的国度。",
    "Your lantern goes down through the still water and finds stairs descending, and doorways, and a street below the street, all of it built to be entered from further down.": "灯光穿过静水向下，照见下降的阶梯、一道道门和街道下方的另一条街；这一切都为从更深处进入者而建。",
    "The foundation holds no rubble and no ruin, for nothing here has fallen: it was built finished, from the bottom up, and left waiting.": "地基中没有碎石，也没有废墟，因为这里从未有东西倒塌；它自下而上完整建成，然后被留在此处等待。",
    "A drowned gallery runs off level and true for as far as the light throws, its ceiling worked with a care no floor is given, cut to be admired from the water's own floor.": "一条被淹长廊平直延伸到灯光尽头，天花板精雕细琢，远胜任何地面；它本就是供人从水底向上欣赏的。",
    "The cold of the foundation is the cold of the deepest water; it rises through the stone into your hands, for the stone was laid to carry it upward.": "地基的寒冷如同最深的水，沿石头传入双手；这些石块铺设之初就是为了将寒意向上传导。",
    "This floor is upon no map the survey keeps, and no map the wardens kept, and the charts of the whole descent run out at the door above it.": "勘测队与守门人的任何地图上都没有这一层；整段下行的图表在上方那扇门处便已终止。",
    "Whatever passed the last door was entered outward bound in the Roll above, in the firm hand of its season: the return column against every such entry stands open to this day.": "凡是穿过最后一扇门的东西，都由当季有力笔迹在上方名册登记为离境；与每条记录对应的归还栏至今仍然空着。",
    "The stone of the floor takes no mark: your chalk leaves no line upon it, your boot leaves no print, the floor keeps no record of your passing.": "地面石头不接受任何痕迹：粉笔画不出线，靴子踩不下印，这一层拒绝记录你的经过。",
    "The walls are dressed and blank, cut for tablets that were never let; the niches for lamps stand empty, for the floor was never meant to be written.": "墙面修整平滑而空白，留有安装铭板的凹位，却从未刻出铭板；灯龛也空着，因为这一层从来不打算留下文字。",
    "You find a surveyor's sighting-frame abandoned at the floor's edge, its sights trained down into the dark, its field-book beside it holding one blank page and no more.": "地面边缘遗弃着测量员的观测架，瞄具对准下方黑暗；旁边的野外记录簿只剩一页空白，此后再无纸张。",
    "The mill stands at the head of the race with its wheel stopped and its stones still in gear, and the race runs under it and turns nothing at all.": "磨坊立在引水渠上游，水轮停转，磨石却仍啮合；渠水从下方流过，什么也没有带动。",
    "You come upon a hunting-horn hung upon a thorn at the crossing of two rides, polished and dry and lately used, with the Count's crow cut into the mount.": "两条林间道交叉处，一只猎号挂在荆棘上，光亮干燥，近期才有人使用；号角饰座刻着伯爵的乌鸦。",
    "Owl-light comes early under the thorn, and the wood goes quiet in one movement, the way a room goes quiet when a door opens behind you.": "荆棘下早早降临猫头鹰活动的昏光，树林会在同一瞬间安静下来，就像身后房门突然打开时整间屋子一齐噤声。",
    "The Bone Orchard is a burying-ground planted as an orchard, apple upon every grave, and the trees are old and heavy and bear every year without fail.": "白骨果园是一片按果园种植的墓地，每座坟上都有一棵苹果树；树木苍老沉重，却年年结果，从不失约。",
    "The abbey of Saint Ordel stands roofless at the head of the orchard, its tower down across the nave, and its bell in the rubble where the tower left it.": "圣奥德尔修道院无顶地立在果园上方，塔楼横倒在中殿，钟则留在塔楼坠落处的瓦砾中。",
    "The graves are dug in rows and the rows are numbered, and the numbering is complete, and there are more numbers cut than there are stones standing.": "坟墓成排挖掘，各排编号齐全；刻出的编号却比仍立着的墓碑更多。",
    "Windfalls lie under every tree in a red drift, unbruised and untouched, and no crow of the Vale will come into the orchard to take one.": "每棵树下都堆着红色落果，完好无碰伤；山谷里的乌鸦没有一只肯飞进果园啄食。",
    "The abbey's register lies open upon the lectern under the open sky, and the rain has not touched the page, and the page is a page of baptisms.": "修道院名册在露天斜面书架上摊开，雨水却没有沾湿纸页；翻开的正是一页洗礼记录。",
    "One grave in the orchard is dug and lined and empty, kept clear of leaves and turned over every season by a spade no one in the Vale will own to.": "果园中有一座墓穴已挖好、砌好却仍空着，里面不见落叶；每个赛季都有一把山谷中无人肯认领的铲子重新翻土。",
    "The consecration of this ground was struck out of the diocesan books by a hand that pressed hard enough to go through three leaves.": "这片土地的祝圣记录被人从教区簿册中划去，下笔之重穿透了三张纸。",
    "The apples of the orchard keep the smell of the cellar rather than the smell of the tree, and they are cold to the hand at any hour of the day.": "果园苹果散发的是地窖气味，而非树木气息；无论白天哪个时辰，摸上去都冷得刺骨。",
    "The Weeping Fen lies in the floor of the Vale, and the black water of Ysmere lies in the middle of the fen, and neither has a bottom the village will name.": "哭泣沼泽位于山谷低处，伊斯梅尔的黑水又位于沼泽中央；两者都深不见底，村民不肯说出底下是什么。",
    "Reeds stand black and dense in every direction and part before you and close behind you, and the path through them is a path you make and lose.": "芦苇向四面八方漆黑密集，在你面前分开，又在身后合拢；穿行其中的路由你开辟，也随即消失。",
    "The water of Ysmere is still enough to hold the crag and the castle upon it whole and upside down, and the reflection is clearer than the crag itself.": "伊斯梅尔的水面静得足以完整倒映峭壁与其上的城堡，倒影甚至比峭壁本身更清晰。",
    "Wedding linen hangs bleaching upon the reeds a mile from any house, white and wet and laid out to dry in a country that has no sun to dry it.": "离任何房屋一英里外，芦苇上挂着婚礼用的白布，湿淋淋地摊开晾晒；这里却没有太阳能把它晒干。",
    "A drowned causeway runs out into the lake and stops, and the stones of it are dressed and pinned, and it was built to reach the middle and got there.": "一条被淹没的堤道伸入湖中后戛然而止；石块修整并固定得很牢，它原本就是要通到湖心，而且确实到了那里。",
    "The fen weeps in the proper sense of the word, for water rises out of the peat wherever a boot presses, and it rises warm.": "沼泽名副其实地在哭泣：靴子踩下之处，水便从泥炭中涌出，而且温热。",
    "Bells sound out of the lake at intervals, deep and slow and very far down, and they keep the ringing of a wedding rather than the ringing of a burial.": "湖中不时传来钟声，低沉、缓慢，仿佛来自极深之处；那是婚礼的钟，而非葬礼的钟。",
    "Rings lie in the shallows in numbers, plain silver and worn thin, every one of them a wedding-ring, and every one of them cut through.": "浅水中散落着许多戒指，都是磨薄的素银婚戒，而且每一枚都被切断。",
    "The peat gives up its keeping wherever a boot presses hard: a shoe, a comb, a hand of cards, all of them sodden and none of them rotted.": "靴子用力踩下之处，泥炭便吐出它保存的东西：鞋子、梳子、一手纸牌，全都湿透，却没有腐烂。",
    "You wade a channel that was not there yesterday and will not be there tomorrow, for the fen moves its water about in the night like a householder shifting furniture.": "你涉过一条昨日尚不存在、明日也不会存在的水道；沼泽在夜里搬动水流，就像屋主挪动家具。",
    "A drowned hedge runs out into the lake in a straight line for two hundred yards, laid and pleached by a hedger who worked this ground when it was field.": "一排被淹的树篱沿直线伸入湖中两百码；它由这片土地还是田野时的篱笆匠栽植编结而成。",
    "The reeds carry a smell of cut flowers a mile from any garden, and it comes strongest where the water is deepest and the linen hangs.": "离任何花园一英里外，芦苇间仍飘着剪下花朵的气味；水越深、婚布悬挂之处越浓。",
    "Frogs go quiet in a wave across the whole fen at once, from the far bank to your boots, and take a full minute to start again.": "蛙声如波浪般从远岸一路沉寂到你的靴边，整片沼泽同时安静下来；过足一分钟后才重新响起。",
    "The lake gives back the crag and the castle upside down and perfect, and gives back nothing of you at all, though you stand at the very edge of it.": "湖面完美倒映出倒置的峭壁与城堡，却完全不映出你，尽管你就站在水边。",
    "The curtain wall of Corvane rings the crag entire, and the breach in it was made from the inside, and the stone lies outward down the slope.": "科尔瓦恩的环城墙包围整座峭壁，墙上缺口却是从内侧破开的；石块向外滚落山坡。",
    "The kennels stand against the wall in a long row of forty runs, and the runs are swept, and the straw is fresh, and thirty-nine of the gates stand open.": "犬舍沿城墙排成四十间长列，每间都打扫干净，铺着新鲜稻草；其中三十九扇门敞开着。",
    "The feeding-trough of the kennels is filled to the hour by a hand that keeps the hour, and the meat in it is fresh, and there is no butcher in the Vale.": "犬舍食槽由准时守候的手按时填满，肉仍然新鲜；可山谷中根本没有屠夫。",
    "A hunting-board is nailed inside the gate with the season's meets written up in a fair hand, and the last entry upon it is dated for tomorrow.": "大门内钉着狩猎公告板，工整记录本赛季的集合地点；最后一条日期写的是明天。",
    "The gatehouse portcullis is up and pinned, and the pins are greased, and the winding-gear turns under one hand as smoothly as a well-kept lock.": "门楼吊闸升起并固定，插销涂过油；绞盘齿轮在一只手下转动顺滑，如保养良好的锁。",
    "Kennel-hounds bay from somewhere below the wall in a body, all at once and then all silent, the way a pack answers a horn it has been taught.": "城墙下方某处传来一群猎犬齐声吠叫，随后同时噤声，就像受训犬群回应号角。",
    "The stable-yard holds one coach with its lamps trimmed and its harness laid out ready, and the coach has neither horses in it nor dust upon it.": "马厩院里停着一辆马车，灯芯修好，挽具整齐摆放待用；车上没有马，也没有一粒尘土。",
    "From the wall-walk the whole Vale lies below you under its mist, village and wood and orchard and fen, and every road in it runs to the crag you stand on.": "站在城墙步道上，整座山谷都在雾下铺展：村庄、树林、果园与沼泽，所有道路都通向你脚下的峭壁。",
    "The armoury within the gatehouse is racked and oiled and complete, and every weapon in it is set with its edge toward the door.": "门楼内军械库的武器架齐全而上油，每件兵器都将刃口朝向大门摆放。",
    "A tally of the pack is chalked upon the kennel wall in a fair hand and corrected daily, and today's figure is thirty-nine, and there are forty runs.": "犬舍墙上用端正字迹写着犬群计数，每日修正；今日数字是三十九，而犬舍共有四十间。",
    "The wall-walk is swept from end to end, and the sweepings are heaped tidily at the stair-head where somebody means to come back for them.": "城墙步道从头到尾都被扫过，垃圾整齐堆在阶梯口，仿佛有人打算回来取走。",
    "Bells are hung along the inside of the curtain at intervals, on wires that run inward to the house, and every one of them is a bell for going out rather than for coming in.": "环城墙内侧每隔一段便挂着钟，细线向内连入宅邸；每一口钟都用于外出，而非进门。",
    "A brazier at the wall-head holds a fire banked and living, and there is a stack of split wood beside it cut to the length of the brazier, seasoned two years.": "城墙顶端火盆里的炉火压得低却仍在燃烧，旁边堆着按火盆长度劈好的木柴，已经风干两年。",
    "The mist stands level with the wall-walk and goes no higher, so that the crag is an island and the whole of the Vale beneath it is under water that is not water.": "雾气与城墙步道齐平，不再升高；峭壁仿佛一座岛，而下方整座山谷都被并非真正的水淹没。",
    "Castle Corvane is kept: the floors are swept, the glass is clean, the fires are laid, and the house has had no servants for three hundred years.": "科尔瓦恩城堡仍被维护：地板清扫干净，玻璃明亮，炉火架好；然而这座宅邸已有三百年没有仆人。",
    "Covers are off the furniture in every room of the state floor, and the covers are folded and stacked, and the folding is recent and done to a housekeeper's standard.": "正层每个房间的家具都揭去了罩布，罩布折叠后整齐堆放；折痕很新，手法如专业管家所为。",
    "The long gallery hangs with portraits of one family in its generations, and the same man stands in the corner of every canvas, and he does not age between them.": "长廊挂满同一家族历代肖像，每幅画角落都站着同一个男人，而他在画与画之间从未老去。",
    "A place is laid at the head of the great table for one, with the plate turned down and the glass turned up, and it has been laid this way since the burial.": "长桌首位为一人摆好餐具，盘子倒扣、酒杯正立；自葬礼以来，它一直保持这个样子。",
    "The chapel of the castle is shuttered from within and its door wedged with a beam, and the wedge was set by someone standing on the inside.": "城堡礼拜堂从内部关上百叶窗，门也用横梁楔住；横梁是站在里面的人放置的。",
    "Music is played in the music-room at the same hour every evening, one instrument and one air, and the air is a wedding air played at half the pace it was written for.": "音乐室每天同一时刻都会奏乐，一件乐器、一支曲调；那是婚礼曲，却以谱写速度的一半缓慢演奏。",
    "The great stair is carpeted and the carpet is worn in one track only, up the middle, by three hundred years of one man's feet going up and coming down.": "大阶梯铺着地毯，中央只有一道磨损路线，是同一个人的双脚三百年来上下走出的痕迹。",
    "The Count's own chamber stands open at the head of the stair, and the bed in it is made, and it has never once been slept in.": "伯爵的寝室敞开在阶梯顶端，床铺整齐，却从未有人睡过一次。",
    "The kitchens are laid out for a household of forty: coppers scoured, spits greased, the great table floured for pastry that nobody has come down to make.": "厨房按四十人的宅邸配置：铜锅擦亮，烤叉上油，大桌撒好面粉，却没人下来制作糕点。",
    "A clock upon the landing keeps the right hour and is wound every eight days by a hand you never meet, and its case has been opened so often the varnish is worn about the key-hole.": "楼梯平台上的钟走时准确，每八天由一只你从未遇见的手上弦；钟壳开得太频繁，钥匙孔周围的清漆都磨掉了。",
    "The library is catalogued and shelved and the ladders are set where a reader left them, and the book upon the reading-desk is open at a page about the keeping of hounds.": "图书馆目录齐全，书架井然，梯子停在读者离开的位置；阅读桌上的书翻在讲述猎犬饲养的一页。",
    "Linen is aired upon a horse before the fire in a room with no bed in it, and it is aired again the next day, and the day after that.": "没有床的房间里，一匹木马前对着炉火晾着亚麻布；第二天、再下一天，它仍被重新晾晒。",
    "The great hall's fires are laid but never lit, kindling under split logs under a taper, in every one of the six hearths, and the tapers are new.": "大厅六座壁炉都架好了炉火却从不点燃，细柴置于劈木和引火蜡烛下；蜡烛还是新的。",
    "Water stands ready in the ewers of every guest chamber on the state floor, fresh drawn, and there has not been a guest in this house since the burial.": "正层每间客房的水壶都备着刚打来的清水；可自葬礼以来，这座宅邸从未接待过客人。",
    "Somewhere below the state floor a door closes, without hurry and without violence, the way a door closes behind somebody who lives there.": "正层下方某处有门合上，不急不躁，也不带暴力，仿佛住在里面的人顺手关门。",
    "The court's antechambers stand flooded to the knee, and the water carries the smell of the drowned temple down from above.": "宫廷前厅积水没膝，水里带着从上方溺没神殿传下来的气味。",
    "A tide-mark of candle grease rings the pillars at the height of a man's shoulder.": "蜡油潮痕环绕柱身，正好在人类肩膀高度。",
    "Somewhere below the water a bell is ringing, slow and patient, in a tower drowned before Mereward was named.": "水下某处钟声缓慢而耐心地响着，来自梅里沃德得名之前便已沉没的高塔。",
    "The court's clerks pole between the pillars upon rafts of coffin-wood, keeping the season's minutes dry.": "宫廷书记员站在棺木扎成的木筏上，在柱间撑船，努力让本赛季的会议记录保持干燥。",
    "The season's docket is nailed to a pillar above the flood, its lower half already dark and swollen with the rising water.": "本赛季事项表钉在洪水之上的柱子上，下半部已经因上涨的水浸黑、泡胀。",
    "Coffins ride the antechamber upright, weighted at the foot, standing among the pillars like a gallery of the accused awaiting their call.": "棺材竖立在前厅，底部压着重物，站在柱间，像一排等待点名的被告。",
    "The drowned bell tolls the court to session, and each stroke comes up muffled through the water a moment after the last has died.": "溺钟召唤宫廷开庭，每一下钟声都在上一声消失片刻后，隔着水闷闷传来。",
    "The water has risen a hand's breadth since your descent began, and the lowest step of the dais now stands awash before the empty throne.": "自你开始下行以来，水位上涨了一掌宽；高台最低一级如今已淹在空王座前的水中。",
    "Grave-lilies float in drifts against the pillars, cut and cast upon the water fresh for the sitting.": "墓百合成片漂在柱边，是为本次开庭新剪下、撒入水中的。",
    "Goblin tally-marks are scratched fresh beside the court's door, and the newest of them are still white in the stone.": "宫廷门旁新刻着哥布林计数痕，最新几道仍在石头上泛白。",
    "The drums have come down from the warren, and their ragged rhythm carries through all the floors between.": "鼓声从巢穴一路传下，破碎的节奏穿过其间所有楼层。",
    "A dirty grey flag hangs above the stair: the warren has sent its heralds even here.": "阶梯上方挂着肮脏的灰旗：巢穴甚至把使者派到了这里。",
    "Small eyes watch the court's proceedings from the murder-holes, and small wagers change hands upon your progress.": "一双双小眼睛从射孔里窥视宫廷审理，随着你的进展，小额赌注不断易手。",
    "The goblins keep the court's own hours now, and a runner beats the changes of the watch upon a drum at the stair-head.": "哥布林如今按宫廷时刻行动，传令者在阶梯口击鼓报出换岗时辰。",
    "A tree of trophies stands raised beside the court door in the warren fashion, hung with helms and tags taken off the deep.": "宫廷门旁立着一棵按巢穴样式搭成的战利品树，挂满从深处取来的头盔和编号牌。",
    "Watch-fires burn on the landings in a climbing line, tended in turn, so the whole stair up to the court is held and lit.": "平台上的警戒火沿阶梯向上排列，轮流有人看守；通往宫廷的整段阶梯因此被守住，也被照亮。",
    "The tally beside the door is amended as you climb, a fresh mark cut for each floor you clear, the marks grouped by sevens.": "你每清理一层，门旁计数便增添一道新痕，刻痕按七分组。",
    "A herald in grey rag stands upon the newel and cries your rank and your road down to the court below, in a tongue of clicks and drum-taps.": "一名披灰布的传令者站在柱头，用弹舌声与鼓点向下方宫廷宣告你的阶位和下行路线。",
    "The funeral lamps burn in every niche of the stair, lit in their thousands by no hand the court will name.": "阶梯每个壁龛都燃着葬灯，成千上万盏灯不知由哪只宫廷不愿提名的手点亮。",
    "The lamplight stands steady in air where your torch gutters, and by that light the barrow-dead go about the court's business.": "你的火把摇曳不定，葬灯的光却在空气中稳定燃烧；墓中亡者借其光线处理宫廷事务。",
    "Wax runs warm down stones that were cold for an age, and the smell of it is almost that of a chapel.": "蜡油温热地流过曾寒冷一个时代的石头，气味几乎像一座礼拜堂。",
    "Your shadow falls in four directions at once upon the stair, and only one of them keeps your pace.": "你的影子同时投向阶梯四个方向，却只有一道影子与你步调一致。",
    "The lamps are trimmed and refilled ahead of your climb, niche by niche, and the oil in every one stands level to the drop.": "你上行前，灯火已逐龛修剪并添油；每盏灯的油面都恰好齐平。",
    "The barrow-dead go up and down the stair on the court's errands, keeping to the wall by an old courtesy, their grave-lamps needing no hand to trim them.": "墓中亡者为宫廷差事上下阶梯，出于古老礼节靠墙行走；他们的墓灯无需人手修剪。",
    "The wax has run and set down the stones in long pale falls, layer upon layer, the record of a great many sittings kept by lamplight.": "蜡油在石上流淌凝固成一道道苍白长痕，层层叠叠，记录着许多次灯下开庭。",
    "A lamplighter's pole stands leaned in a niche, its wick yet smoking, though the hand that set it there has gone on up ahead of you.": "点灯杆斜靠在壁龛中，灯芯仍冒着烟；放下它的手却已经走到你前方。",
    "The flames burn straight and tall in the draught that gutters your own torch, drawn steady toward the court above.": "气流让你的火把摇曳，灯焰却挺直高燃，稳定地朝上方宫廷延伸。",
    "A procession of the risen dead passes through the court by an appointed route, bearing grave-goods before them in the old order.": "一列复生亡者按既定路线穿过宫廷，依古老次序在队伍前方抬着墓中物品。",
    "The procession halts while you pass, by some instruction of precedence, and the empty helms turn to mark you.": "依照某条尊卑规矩，队伍在你经过时停下；空头盔齐齐转向你。",
    "Grave-flowers of pale silk are strewn along the processional way, and they are fresh.": "浅色丝绸制成的墓花撒满行进路线，花朵仍然新鲜。",
    "The wyrm's mark is burned into the shoulder of every walker in the procession, and the brand is newer than the grave-clothes.": "队伍中每名行者肩上都烙着巨龙印记，烙痕比身上的寿衣还新。",
    "The procession keeps a slow drum at its head, and the dead step to it in a time older than the tune the drum beats.": "队伍前方维持着缓慢鼓点，亡者踏着节拍行走；这节拍比鼓声所奏的曲调更加古老。",
    "Grave-goods are borne before the walkers on biers in the old order, the greater houses' silver first and the lesser behind.": "墓中物品按古老次序由灵柩架抬在队伍前方，大户人家的银器在先，小户随后。",
    "The route of the procession is set into the floor in worn brass studs, a circuit that returns upon itself and never leaves the court.": "队伍路线以磨损的黄铜钉嵌在地板上，是一条在宫廷内自我回转、从不离开的环线。",
    "A place is kept empty in the ranks, a bier shouldered with nothing upon it, dressed and carried as though its tenant walked there still.": "队列中留着一个空位，一具肩抬的灵柩上什么也没有，却仍被装饰并抬行，仿佛其中住客尚在行走。",
    "The risen halt as one to let you by, and the helms turn to follow you, and the drum keeps its beat through the pause without a stumble.": "复生者齐齐停下让你通过，头盔随后转向追随你；停顿期间鼓点没有丝毫踉跄。",
    "Things come up the stair from below to test the new warden, and are turned back at the last door, one by one, as they were turned back before you.": "有东西从下方沿阶梯上来考验新守门人，却像你之前的来客一样，一个接一个在最后一扇门前被击退。",
    "The jar stands upon its mantel in the vault above, centred and dusted, and the fire beneath it is laid and not lit, as you keep it.": "上方宝库里，罐子端正无尘地立在壁炉架中央；下方炉火已架好却未点燃，正如你一直维持的样子。",
    "The seventh seal hangs whole upon the vault wall, the six struck through in lead beside it, and you have entered your own name at the head of the new Roll.": "第七枚封印完整挂在宝库墙上，旁边六枚已用铅划销；你则在新名册开头登记了自己的名字。",
    "The windlass turns at the rim far above, and the Guild sends down the next name upon the roll, and you examine it at the door and send it home.": "遥远上方边缘的绞盘开始转动，行会把名册上的下一个名字送下来；你在门口查验后将它送回。",
    "A claimant reaches the sill in the dark, finds the door kept and the count entered against it, and goes back down the way it came.": "一名索债者在黑暗中抵达门槛，发现大门有人守着、计数也已登记，便沿来路退回下方。",
    "The water stands where it lay, driven back and held, and the drum keeps its count in sevens under the works, and you keep the works.": "水被推回并拦住，仍停在原处；工场下方的鼓以七为组维持计数，而你守护着工场。",
    "The first hoard lies warm and quiet at the bottom, the debt bound anew beneath it, and the glow of it dims and steadies as the breathing slows.": "最初的宝藏温暖而安静地躺在最底层，债务重新被束缚在下方；随着呼吸放缓，光芒渐暗并稳定下来。",
    "You walk the offices of the keeping on your rounds, the Roll and the gallery and the debtors' deep, and you find the wardens' work sound and add your own to it.": "巡查时，你走过守护机构的各处：名册、长廊与债务人深处；守门人的工程仍然稳固，你也把自己的工作添了进去。",
    "The chair at the last door is worn to its sitter through an age of sitting, and it is yours now, and the count is yours, and the season turns.": "最后一扇门旁的椅子历经一个时代，被坐出主人的轮廓；如今它属于你，计数也属于你，赛季开始轮转。",
    "You make the circuit of the seven this season, from the sealed door above the crypts to the vault below the court, mending what has worked loose since the last sitting.": "本赛季你巡行七处，从墓穴上方的封门走到宫廷下方的宝库，修补上次开庭以来松动的部分。",
    "A seal has slipped a hair at the elder stair, where the wyrm's weight is off it, and you set it true and enter the mending in the Roll.": "古老阶梯处的一道封印在巨龙重量移开后偏了一丝；你将它校正，并把修补记录进名册。",
    "The lead of the struck seals is renewed where the damp has crept, six of them, and the seventh left whole, as the last warden kept it.": "潮气侵蚀之处，六枚划销封印上的铅被重新补好；第七枚仍保持完整，一如上一位守门人的安排。",
    "The great chain lies bound again across the chained dark, its parted links drawn to and pinned, and the anchors hold, and you sign the mending beneath the seven hands.": "巨链再次横缚锁链黑暗，裂开的链环被拉拢固定，锚点依然稳固；你在七份笔迹下签署修补记录。",
    "The works have gone a hair out of true with the season's water, and you weigh the counterweight afresh, and the drum takes up its count in sevens again.": "工场因本季水量出现一丝偏差；你重新校准配重，鼓声便再次以七为组开始计数。",
    "The gallery of the seven keeps its six tenants and its nameless eighth, and you dust the effigies on your round and leave the chalk where it lies.": "七人长廊仍守着六位住客与无名的第八座墓；巡查时你拂去雕像灰尘，却让粉笔留在原处。",
    "A weakness shows in the foundation where the drowned stone was worked from below, and you shore it and enter the figure, and the deep holds.": "从下方开凿的淹没石工处显出一处薄弱点；你加以支撑、登记数值，深渊依旧稳固。",
    "The manifest of the sealed is brought current in your own hand, every warden entered and every warden struck, and a place ruled clean for the name that keeps the count next.": "你亲手把封印名录更新到当前：每位守门人都已登记并划销，另留一格空白，等待下一个维持计数的名字。",
    "The audit closes sound, the seven mended and the count kept, and you climb back to the chair at the last door with the season entered fair.": "审计以一切稳固作结：七处已修补，计数仍维持；你将本季端正入册，回到最后一扇门旁的椅子。",
    "The Guild writes to its warden this season, and sends down the next enrolment of adventurers with their numbered tags, to be examined at the door and sent home.": "本赛季行会写信给守门人，并把下一批带编号牌的登记冒险者送下来，让你在门前查验后遣返。",
    "A letter comes down the stair in a runner's hand, the Guild's own seal upon it, asking after the count and the seals and the health of the deep, and you answer it fair.": "信使沿阶梯送来一封盖着行会印章的信，询问计数、封印与深渊状况；你一一端正作答。",
    "The next names upon the roll arrive at the last door, blinking in your lamp, and you rule them not yet ready and send them up with a word for the Guildmaster.": "名册上的下一批人来到最后一扇门，在灯光下眨着眼；你判定他们尚未准备好，托话给行会长后送回上方。",
    "The windlass turns above for each name sent home, and the Guild enters the examining, and the deep keeps one fewer numbered tag to fill.": "每遣返一个名字，上方绞盘便转动一次；行会登记查验结果，深渊也少留下一枚待填的编号牌。",
    "You keep a fair copy of every letter from above in the new Roll, that the warden after you may read what passed between the deep and the surface in your season.": "你在新名册中端正誊抄每封来自上方的信，好让继任守门人读到本季深渊与地表间发生的往来。",
    "A tag comes down the stair with no adventurer behind it, recovered from some floor and sent to its warden, and you enter it and set it by.": "一枚编号牌独自沿阶梯送来，身后没有冒险者；它从某层寻回，交还守门人，你登记后将其收好。",
    "The jar keeps its place on the mantel through the reading and the writing both, the fire laid and unlit, and the count holds.": "无论读信还是写信，罐子始终留在壁炉架原位，炉火架好却未点燃，计数保持不变。",
    "The Guild's letters grow easy in their tone as the season turns, for the deep is quiet under a keeper who keeps it, and they say so, and you enter that too.": "随着赛季轮转，行会来信的语气愈发轻松，因为深渊在尽职守门人手下保持安静；信中如此写道，你也将其登记。",
    "The last letter of the season goes up the windlass in your own hand, the count reported sound, and you take the chair at the door again and wait upon the next.": "本季最后一封信以你的笔迹随绞盘送上，报告计数无误；你再次坐回门旁椅子，等待下一季。",
    "The debt beneath turns in its new bonds this season, and the drum wants re-weighting, and you set the counterweight true and keep the count at the door.": "本赛季下方债务在新束缚中翻身，鼓的配重需要重调；你校准配重，并在门前维持计数。",
    "The glow at the bottom brightens a shade as the debt stirs in its sleep, and dims again as the bonds hold, and you enter the stirring in the Roll.": "债务在睡梦中翻动时，最底层光芒微微增强；束缚稳住后又暗下来，你将这次异动记入名册。",
    "A tremor comes up the stair from the Bottom, felt through the chair and the floor, and it is the debt turning, and the bonds hold, and the count is kept.": "一道震颤从最底层沿阶梯传来，经椅子与地板进入身体；那是债务在翻身，但束缚稳固，计数仍在维持。",
    "The water tries the seal where the debt breathes hardest against it, and the works drive it back, and the drum keeps its sevens, and the works hold against the breathing.": "债务呼吸最重之处，水流冲击封印；工场将其压回，鼓继续数着一组组七，机械抵住了呼吸。",
    "The first hoard lies warm at the bottom, the debt bound beneath it, and the coin shifts and rings as the great thing turns, and settles as it sleeps.": "最初的宝藏温热地躺在底部，债务被缚在其下；庞然之物翻身时金币移动作响，沉睡后又归于平静。",
    "You go down on your rounds to the waking ground and read the count in the bedrock, seven and seven, and the bright new mark is your own, cut this season.": "巡查时你下到苏醒之地，阅读基岩上七个又七个的计数；那道明亮新痕由你在本季亲手刻下。",
    "The debt sends the count up the stair to be told, as it has told every warden down, and you tell it back, and it settles, for a keeper answers where a corpse cannot.": "债务沿阶梯把计数送上来诉说，一如它曾向每位守门人诉说；你把数字报回去，它便安定下来，因为守门人会回答，尸体不会。",
    "The bonds you set upon the debt hold through the turning, closed link to link as the wardens closed them, and you sign the holding beneath the seven hands.": "你施加在债务上的束缚经受住翻动，链环如历代守门人所做般逐一闭合；你在七份笔迹下签字确认。",
    "The count at the door is kept another season, the debt bound and the deep held, and you climb to the chair with the season entered and the jar upon its mantel above.": "门前计数又维持一个赛季，债务受缚，深渊守住；你登记本季后回到椅子，上方罐子仍在壁炉架上。",
    "The Guild charts the dead floors at leisure this season, floor by floor, and the chains are measured for salvage, and what walks among the surveyors is remnant and echo.": "本赛季行会从容测绘已经死去的楼层，一层接一层；锁链被量作回收之用，而行走在测量员之间的只是残余与回声。",
    "The glow is gone from the Bottom, and the coin lies cold, and the surveyors chart it by lamplight, and it is only a hoard now, and they weigh it as one.": "最底层光芒已经消失，金币冰冷躺着；测量员借灯光绘图，如今它只是一座宝藏，他们也按宝藏称量。",
    "The drum is silent under the works, and the water stands where it lay, and the surveyors sound the still galleries and enter them stone by stone.": "工场下方鼓声沉寂，水停留原处；测量员勘测安静长廊，一块石头一块石头地登记。",
    "The great chain is measured for salvage along its slack miles, the parted links tallied, and the seven signatures at the anchors copied for the library before the iron is drawn up.": "绵延数英里的松弛巨链被测量以供回收，裂开链环逐一计数；铁链拉上去前，锚点上的七份签名被誊抄送往图书馆。",
    "A remnant crosses the survey's line in the dark, thin and aimless, and is turned aside with a lamp and a word, and it drifts back the way it came.": "一道稀薄、漫无目的的残影在黑暗中越过测量线，被一盏灯和一句话引开，又沿来路飘回。"
  });
})();

(function () {
  'use strict';
  Object.assign(globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT, {
    "a wrapping of tomb-linen": "一裹墓葬亚麻布",
    "A serpent of living fire kept in the Last Vault against the hour the jar is fed to the flame. It coils about the laid hearth, warms the black stone of the vault, and takes any that near the mantel for the tender come at last to light the fire. Its coil sears through mail.": "一条活火构成的巨蛇，被养在最终宝库，等待罐子投入火焰的时刻。它盘绕在铺好的炉床旁，温暖宝库的黑石；任何靠近壁炉架的人，都会被它当成终于前来点火的司炉。它的盘绕足以灼穿锁甲。",
    "The Lich's own clerk, the last but one upon the Roll, kept at the enrolling of a new season that never comes. It sits the vault's second desk, copies the count in a fair hand, and defends the record before its own unlife. Its inkhorn is dried to a crust in a grip that will not open.": "巫妖自己的书记员，名册上的倒数第二人，永远守着一场不会到来的新赛季登记。它坐在宝库的第二张书桌前，以工整笔迹誊抄数目，并把记录看得比自己的不死之身更重要。紧握不放的手中，墨角早已干结成壳。",
    "The warden of the seven seals hung upon the vault wall, that strikes each through in lead as its warden falls and keeps the seventh whole. It fights to keep the seventh seal from the striking, for the striking of the seventh is the count left off. Its signet-die cuts the impression of a door that opens once.": "宝库墙上悬着七道封印，它便是封印守卫。每当一名守门人倒下，它会以铅划销对应封印，唯独保持第七道完整。它为阻止第七封印被划销而战，因为划掉第七道，便意味着清点终止。它的印玺模具刻着一扇只能开启一次的门。",
    "A three-armed eater of the deep stone and its treasures, come up through the black walls of the Last Vault by the smell of the hoard below. It takes coin and gem and the metal of a blade alike, rising through the floor to feed and sinking back when it is full. Stone is no wall to it.": "三臂的深石吞食者，被下方宝藏的气味吸引，穿过最终宝库的黑墙而来。钱币、宝石和刀刃金属在它口中并无分别；它从地面升起进食，饱足后再沉回去。石头对它从来不是墙壁。",
    "A shade of the dark that pours over the sill of the last door with the reversed water. It keeps to the threshold no warden crossed living, and it draws the warmth from those who cross where it has pooled. It belongs to the door, and a caller who wins past the sill is quit of it.": "一道黑暗之影，随逆流水越过最后一扇门的门槛倾泻而下。它守着那道没有守门人活着跨过的门槛，从踏入积影者身上抽走热量。它属于那扇门；只要来客闯过门槛，便能摆脱它。",
    "A low grey crawler that keeps the very brink of the broken seal, where the reversed water goes over and down. It has fed at that edge since the water first went over, and it fastens on a boot at the sill and hauls, to send its meat after the water into the drop.": "低矮灰色的爬行怪，守在破裂封印的最边缘，逆流水从那里翻落向下。自水流第一次越过边缘起，它便一直在那里进食；它会在门槛扣住靴子用力拖拽，让血肉追随水流坠入深处。",
    "A mass of drowned matter gathered together and given a slow will by the water that pours forever over the sill. It drifts down the wet stone in the shape of a man face-down, and it winds about the legs of a wader and bears the weight downward.": "一团溺亡物质聚合在一起，被永远越过门槛的水流赋予迟缓意志。它以面朝下的人形沿湿石漂移，缠住涉水者双腿，把全部重量向下拖去。",
    "A thing born of the water driven back on every floor above and let go at last over the sill. It runs in the sheet of the fall, shaped like nothing the eye can fix upon, and it strikes with the whole weight of the water behind it before it goes on down.": "上方每一层被逼退的水汇聚成这只怪物，最终越过门槛获得释放。它在瀑布般的水幕中奔流，形体无从被目光锁定；它会挟身后全部水重撞击，然后继续向下奔去。",
    "A power of the living rock, woken in the drowned foundation where the oldest stone was worked from below. It rises out of a wall or a floor without warning and returns to it as easily, and its blows carry the mass of the mountain the Maw was dug into.": "活岩之力，在淹没的地基中苏醒；那里最古老的石料曾从下方加工。它会毫无预兆地从墙壁或地面升起，又轻易回归其中；每一击都带着开凿巨口深渊那座山的重量。",
    "A slough of the drowned foundation, shed from the oldest course of stone and gone about on its own account. It fills a gallery from wall to wall in the black water, and what it closes upon it takes down to the bone by degrees.": "从淹没地基最古老的石层剥落而成的泥浆，如今自行游荡。它在黑水中从一面墙铺满到另一面墙；任何被它合围的东西，都会被逐层腐蚀，直至白骨。",
    "A mason-thing of the far side, drowned at the raising of the foundation and raising it yet, that cuts the deepest stone upward toward a surface it will never reach. It defends the course it is cutting against any that near it, and its inverted chisel swings with the reach of a thing built to cut above its own head.": "来自地基另一侧的石匠怪，在地基升起时溺亡，至今仍继续砌筑。它向上凿削最深处的石头，朝着永远无法抵达的地表前进。任何靠近者都会遭到攻击，以保卫它正在修整的石层；倒置凿子挥动的范围，属于一种为头顶作业而生的怪物。",
    "A journeyman of the foundation, drowned at the work and working still, its mallet swinging slow beneath the black water. It keeps to the course it was cutting and defends it, and its mallet falls slow and heavy, timed to a work that has no end.": "地基工场的熟练石匠，劳作时溺亡，如今仍未停工；木槌在黑水下缓慢挥动。它守着并保卫自己正在修整的石层，沉重木槌以缓慢节拍落下，配合一场永无终结的劳作。",
    "A smooth-faced thing of the unwritten floor, featureless as the stone that takes no mark. It keeps no shape the eye can hold and leaves no print, and it presses itself upon a caller to take the marks off them, the face and the name and the record, and to leave them as blank as the floor.": "未书之层的光面怪物，像拒绝留痕的石头一样没有特征。它不维持任何可被目光把握的形体，也不留下脚印；它会贴上来客，抹去其身上的一切标记——面容、姓名与记录——让他们变得像这一层一样空白。",
    "A clerk of the unwritten floor gone as blank as the stone it keeps, that unwrites where a clerk would write. It sets a cold hand upon a caller and lifts the record off them, the ink of a name rising from the skin, and the arm it has read goes slack and slow.": "未书之层的书记员，已经变得和它守护的石头一样空白；普通书记员负责写下，它却负责抹去。冰冷手掌一旦按上来客，便会从其身上揭走记录，姓名的墨迹自皮肤升起，被读取的手臂随即松弛迟缓。",
    "A creeping haze of the unwritten floor that takes the record off whatever it crosses. It moves without haste over the blank stone, and it unwrites a caller the way a wet cloth unwrites a slate, and what it has crossed the floor keeps no memory of.": "未书之层缓慢爬行的薄雾，会抹去沿途一切记录。它不慌不忙地越过空白石面，像湿布擦去石板字迹一样抹消来客；凡被它经过的东西，这一层都不再保留记忆。",
    "A small iron thing of the chained dark, cast off the great chain where a link was drawn open. It scuttles the slack miles on legs of parted links, and it fastens on a caller as a fetter fastens, and it is far stronger than its size, for it is a piece of a thing that broke the world's own chain.": "锁链黑暗中的小型铁怪，从巨链被拉开的链环处剥落。它用断裂链环构成的腿，在绵延数英里的松弛锁链上疾爬，像镣铐一样扣住来客。它的力量远超体形，因为它曾是挣断世界锁链之物的一部分。",
    "A thing walled into the chained dark at an anchor of the great chain, in penance an age gone, and grown into the iron it was chained to. It bides at its anchor where the chain lies slack, and it reaches the length of its parted bond to strike a caller who passes within, cold as the iron and stronger.": "很久以前，这东西为赎罪而被砌进巨链锚点旁的锁链黑暗，如今已与束缚自己的铁融为一体。它守在锁链松垂处的锚点，能沿断裂束缚伸展到极限，攻击进入范围的来客；它像铁一样冰冷，却比铁更强。",
    "A great serpent of the deep dark, thick as a man's waist and crackling with a caged lightning, that has denned in the slack miles of the chain since the fetter parted. It runs the links faster than a horse and swallows its prey whole, and the storm of its breath fills a gallery from wall to wall.": "深暗中的巨蛇，粗如人的腰身，体内囚禁的雷电噼啪作响。自束缚断裂后，它便把绵延数英里的松弛锁链当作巢穴。它沿链环奔行，比马还快，能把猎物整个吞下；吐息掀起的雷暴会从一面墙填满到另一面墙。",
    "A shade of the counting, thin as a scratched line, that keeps to the tally-marks cut into the waking ground. It rises from the cuts in sevens and draws itself across a caller like a mark tallied, and each stroke of it takes a measure of the strength, as a tally takes a measure of a debt.": "计数所生的影子，薄得像一道刻痕，依附在苏醒之地的计数划痕中。它每七道一组从刻痕里升起，像新增账目般划过来客；每一次划击都会量走一份力量，正如计数衡量一份债务。",
    "A warm-plated crawler of the waking ground that lies buried in the bedrock and rouses only when the ground stirs beneath a foot. It comes up where the stone breathes and sinks when the breath falls even, and it strikes with the heat of the deep still in its plates, hot off the glow below.": "苏醒之地的温甲爬行怪，埋在基岩中，只有脚下地面颤动时才会醒来。它从石头呼吸之处升起，呼吸恢复平稳后又沉下；甲片仍保留深处热量，带着下方辉光的新鲜灼热发动攻击。",
    "A great burrower of the waking ground, plated along the back with scales that hold the heat of the deep stone. It swims the bedrock as a fish swims water, drawn upward by the warmth of a living body, and what it closes upon is seared in the closing.": "苏醒之地的巨型掘地兽，背部覆盖着保存深石热量的鳞甲。它像鱼游水般穿行基岩，被活物体温吸引向上；一旦合拢身体，夹在其中的一切都会被灼焦。",
    "A horned thing of the waking ground, kept at the tally the ground has kept since before Mereward. It takes a caller for an error in the count, to be struck out and set right, and it comes on with the whole authority of a sum that must balance.": "苏醒之地的有角怪物，守着一笔比梅里沃德更加古老的大地账目。它把来客视为计数中的错误，必须划掉并纠正；它步步逼近，带着一笔非平衡不可的总账所拥有的全部权威。",
    "A gold-lit shade risen from the warm coin of the Bottom, thin as the glow of the thing breathing beneath. It keeps to the hoard it was struck for, and it pulls the heat out of a caller into the cold gold it wears, and sinks back into the coin when it has fed.": "一道金光照亮的影子，从最底层的温热钱币中升起，像下方呼吸之物的辉光一样单薄。它守着铸造自身的宝藏，将来客体温抽入披在身上的冰冷黄金；进食完毕后，又沉回钱币之中。",
    "A vast blind worm of the deepest deep, the girth of a cart and longer than the eye can follow, that swims the coin of the Bottom as through loose earth. It takes a caller whole with a mouth that fills a gallery, and its sting is a spar of chitin heavy with a venom the sun has never weakened.": "最深处的庞大盲虫，粗如货车，长得让目光也追不到尽头；它在最底层的钱币中游动，如同穿行松土。占满整条长廊的巨口能将来客整个吞下，尾刺则是一根沉重甲壳长矛，盛着从未被阳光削弱的毒液。",
    "The greatest of the debts the deep was dug to bury, risen from the coin at the Bottom to stand between you and the thing beneath it. It is a body grown vast upon the warm hoard, counting, and it fights to keep the last count uncalled, for the calling of it is the collecting.": "这片深渊开凿来掩埋的最大一笔债务，从最底层的钱币中起身，挡在你与下方之物之间。它依温热宝藏长成庞大躯体，不停计数；它为阻止最后一笔账被宣读而战，因为一旦读出，便到了收债之时。",
    "A giant of the first hoard, coin fused into coin in the heat of the thing breathing below, walking on legs of run gold. It strikes with the whole warm mass of the hoard, the coin of it rings at every blow, and it gathers back into the hoard whatever it fells.": "第一批宝藏凝成的巨人。下方呼吸之物的热量将钱币熔为一体，它踏着流金构成的双腿行走。它以整座温热宝藏的质量发动攻击，每一击都令钱币铿然作响；凡被它击倒之物，都会被收回宝藏之中。",
    "A blind, flat-bodied thing of the flooded lower workings, the length of a man's arm and armoured in a slick grey shell. It lies buried in the silt of the sumps until the damp rises through the mine, and then it comes up the seeping galleries to hunt in the wet, sinking back into the silt when the water falls again.": "淹没的下层矿区中，一只无眼扁身怪，长如人的手臂，披着湿滑灰壳。它埋在积水坑淤泥里，等潮气沿矿井上升，便顺渗水长廊爬出，在湿处猎食；水位再次下降时，又沉回淤泥。",
    "A great plated lizard of the deep roads, its back a shield of grey shale grown over long ages. It lies dormant in the rubble of the lower halls, and the tremor of the deep stone rouses it: when the roots of the world shift, the shale-lizard comes grinding up out of the scree to feed.": "深层道路上的巨型甲蜥，背部是经漫长岁月长成的灰色页岩盾甲。它蛰伏于下层厅堂的碎石中，深石震动便会将其唤醒；世界根基一旦移位，页岩蜥就会碾过碎坡钻出，开始进食。",
    "A pale broad-winged thing of the cold manor halls, ragged at the pinion and dusted with frost. It keeps to the lenses and the mirrors, still as a smear of grey, and takes the air only while the breathing dark moves cold through the halls. Where it has passed, the gilt is left rimed and the glass gone white.": "寒冷庄园厅堂里的苍白阔翼怪，飞羽破烂，覆着霜尘。它贴着镜片与镜面静伏，如一抹灰痕；只有会呼吸的黑暗裹着寒气穿过厅堂时，它才振翼升空。所经之处，鎏金结霜，玻璃泛白。",
    "A blind flat-bodied thing of the flooded lower cells, armoured in a rasped grey plate and the length of a tall man. It lies buried in the silt of the debtors' deep until the beam of the sealing-works sets the deep stone shaking, and then it comes grinding up the drowned galleries to hunt while the tremor holds, sinking back into the silt when the beat falls even again.": "淹没的下层牢房中，一只无眼扁身怪，长及高个男子，披着磨粗灰甲。它埋在债务人深渊的淤泥里，直到封印工场的横梁令深石震颤；震动持续时，它便碾过溺水长廊爬出猎食，节拍重新平稳后又沉回淤泥。",
    "A long gold-scaled serpent that swims the warm coin of the Bottom as a snake swims sand, seen only when the deep air lies dead and still and close. It surfaces in the calm to bask in the glow of the thing breathing, its scales struck from the same coin it swims, and it sinks back into the hoard the moment the air stirs. Where it has passed, the coin lies warmer, and the glow shows the track of it a while.": "一条覆金鳞的长蛇，在最底层的温热钱币中游动，如蛇游沙；只有深处空气沉闷、静止、紧闭时才会现身。它在寂静中浮出，沐浴下方呼吸之物的辉光；鳞片与它游过的钱币由同一种黄金铸成。空气一有扰动，它便沉回宝藏。所经之处钱币更加温热，辉光还会暂时映出它的轨迹。"
  });
})();

// Newly added bestiary and system prose from the current game build.
(() => {
  const target = globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT || (globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT = {});
  Object.assign(target, {
    "The window keeps to the itch embed with a boon in force: the boon row added its own height at the smaller embed sizes and could raise a page scrollbar in the middle of a fight, and the log gives that height back now so the window holds its size.": "窗口在 itch 嵌入模式下保持稳定；恩惠生效时，恩惠栏曾在较小嵌入尺寸中额外占高，导致战斗中出现页面滚动条。现在日志会收回这部分高度，窗口尺寸得以保持。",
    "A working of mending. When it fires upon an ill taken on the road, the ill runs a quarter shorter; when a wound carries you below half your HP, it may knit a twentieth of the whole where you stand; and when a boss falls, it may grant +10% speed for a time.": "疗愈法术。道路上的负面效果触发时，其持续时间缩短四分之一；伤口使你的生命值跌破一半时，法术可能当场恢复总量的二十分之一；首领倒下时，还可能暂时赋予速度 +10%。",
    "A working of the old rites. When it fires against the walking dead, the kill is worth half again the experience, and the words stand a while after the thing is down: every stroke lands 15% heavier and the shrug turns another point and a half aside, for a minute. Under the red moon every beast of the floor walks risen, and the rites answer over all of them.": "古老仪式法术。对亡灵触发时，击杀经验提高一半；目标倒下后，仪式效果仍会持续片刻：一分钟内每次攻击伤害提高 15%，并额外减免一点半伤害。红月之下，楼层中的每只野兽都会以亡灵形态出现，仪式对它们全部生效。",
    "Rat-kin of the warren, bred in the middens under the goblin runs and armed with what the goblins throw away. It stands upright to the height of a child, and it fights in numbers for a share of the carrion it guards.": "巢穴鼠人，在哥布林通道下的垃圾堆中繁衍，以哥布林丢弃之物为武器。它直立时只有孩童高，会成群战斗，守护自己分得的腐肉。",
    "Goblins of keener eye are given shortbows and set to watch the approaches. Their arrows fly crooked, but they fly in great number.": "目光敏锐的哥布林会领到短弓，负责监视来路。它们的箭矢飞得歪斜，却数量惊人。",
    "A patient predator that takes the shape of a chest, a door, a barrel: whatever a tired traveller reaches for. The grip of its hide is the grip of hot pitch, and it eats what it holds.": "耐心的捕食者，能化作宝箱、门或木桶，任何疲惫旅人会伸手触碰的东西。它的皮肤像滚烫沥青一样粘住目标，并吞食被它抓住之物。",
    "The watch of the counterfeit town, built of brass and mainspring behind a stamped mask, about a warrant no living clerk has read. It reads the charge aloud to its prisoners, and the sentence is carried out where they stand.": "赝品镇的守卫，冲压面具下是黄铜与发条，奉行一份没有活着的书记员读过的逮捕令。它向囚犯大声宣读罪名，并当场执行判决。",
    "Eagle before and lion behind, proud and carnivorous. The menagerie's stock has hunted its own galleries for a thousand years and knows every perch in the dark.": "前半身是鹰，后半身是狮，骄傲而嗜肉。兽栏中的这一族群在自己的长廊里猎食了千年，熟知黑暗中的每处栖点。",
    "The scriptorium's ink, pooled and self-willed after an age in the warm channels. It takes the shape of whatever was last written in it, and it writes upon flesh as readily as vellum.": "抄写室的墨水，在温暖沟槽中积存了一个时代后获得意志。它会化作最后写入其中的文字，也能像在羊皮纸上一样轻易地写在血肉上。",
    "The unquiet remainder of one who died in the halls and was catalogued rather than buried. Its touch draws the warmth from the living, and doors are nothing to it.": "一名死在厅堂、被编入目录而非下葬者的不安残骸。它的触碰会抽走活人的温度，门对它毫无意义。",
    "A hunting shape of living quicksilver that runs the gallery floors between the mirrors. A blade passes through it and leaves a ripple, and it gathers itself again with the teeth foremost.": "由活水银组成的猎兽，在镜子之间的长廊地面奔行。刀刃穿过它只留下波纹，而它会重新聚拢，獠牙率先成形。",
    "A woman crowned with serpents, whose gaze is death in stone. The figures in her gallery stand in attitudes of flight, and the newest of them are travellers the survey has on its rolls.": "头戴蛇冠的女人，目光能将生命化为石头。她长廊中的雕像都保持着逃跑姿势，其中最新的一尊，正是测绘名册上的旅人。",
    "A servant of poured wax, child-sized, winged after the fashion of a bat and warm to the touch. It runs the master's errands still, and some of the errands are for blood.": "由浇铸蜡制成的仆从，孩童大小，长着蝙蝠般的翅膀，触摸时仍然温热。它继续替主人办事，其中一些差事与鲜血有关。",
    "A man assembled from men, sewn and quickened upon the foundry's tables. It obeys the last order it was given, and the last order was to keep the tables clear.": "由许多人拼装而成的男人，在铸造厂的台面上缝合并唤醒。它服从接到的最后一道命令，而那道命令是清空台面。",
    "A casting quickened before its finishing, one arm short and its face left smooth. It works at its own assembly between watches, with whatever parts come to hand.": "一具尚未完成便被唤醒的铸造体，少了一条手臂，脸部也未刻出五官。它在换岗间隙用手边零件继续组装自己。",
    "The foundry's masterwork in dressed stone, patient as its quarry. It stands among the statuary until the floor trembles, and then the statuary walks.": "铸造厂用整修石材打造的杰作，像采石场一样耐心。它伫立在雕像之间，直到地面震动，然后雕像便开始行走。",
    "An arm of the observatory's great model, drawn off its pivot and gone walking down the gallery. It keeps the sweep it was cut for, turning upon nothing at the height of a man's chest, and it cuts what stands in the arc.": "观测台巨型模型的一条手臂，从轴心脱落后沿长廊行走。它仍按原本切削出的轨迹，在齐胸高度绕着虚无旋转，切开弧线上的一切。",
    "The last and heaviest of the foundry's issue, set to keep the observatory door. It has stood its post since the pouring, and its orders admit no callers.": "铸造厂最后、最沉重的成品，被派来守住观测台大门。自浇铸完成起它便一直守岗，接到的命令是不许任何来客进入。",
    "The office of the court's usher, kept up long after the usher who held it. It stands at the servants' door in a grey livery, hooded and gaunt, and it admits and turns away by a precedence only it now remembers. It strikes those who pass out of their proper order.": "宫廷司礼员的职位，在原本担任它的人死后仍被维持。它穿灰色制服、戴兜帽，瘦削地站在仆役门边，凭唯一记得的尊卑顺序放行或驱逐来客；任何人若不按正确顺序经过，都会遭到攻击。",
    "A patch of living dark that peels itself from a wall the lamps of the empty court have left unlit. It drains the strength from those it touches, and what it drains it keeps. The court's antechambers are thick with them, and they cross no lit ground.": "一片有生命的黑暗，从空置宫廷未被灯火照亮的墙上剥落下来。它吸走接触者的力量，并将吸走之物据为己有。宫廷前厅到处都是这种东西，却从不踏上有光的地面。",
    "The herald of a court that no longer sits, crying the seasons to a room of empty thrones. It gives the order of business in a cracked voice to any who enter, and it takes the interruption of its cry for contempt. Its handbell carries further in the dark than a shout.": "早已不再开庭的宫廷传令员，向空王座之间宣告赛季。任何进入者都会听到它用嘶哑声音宣布议程；若有人打断，它便视为蔑视。它手中的铃声在黑暗中传得比呼喊更远。",
    "The remainder of one who died attending the court and was never entered as departed. It keeps to the antechambers by the road it walked in life, passing through the shut doors of the offices, and its touch ages the living toward their own entry upon the Roll.": "一名死于侍奉宫廷、却从未登记为亡者的残余。它沿生前走过的道路徘徊在前厅，穿过紧闭的办公室门；它的触碰会使活人衰老，直至他们也被登记进名册。",
    "A thing of thread and lead and long habit that binds the volumes of the Roll as they are filled. It works the stacks by the court's endless day, and it binds into its volumes whatever it finds loose among the shelves: a page, a pen, a reader's hand.": "由线、铅与漫长习惯组成的东西，会在名册卷册填满时将其装订。它在宫廷无尽的白昼中整理书架，把架上散落的一切装进卷册：纸页、羽笔，甚至读者的手。",
    "A clerk of the Roll whose own name was entered and then struck through, and who keeps at the enrolling still. It strikes through the living as it was struck, drawing its pale ink across them, and where the ink falls the strength goes out of the limb.": "名册书记员，自己的名字曾被登记又划去，却仍继续登记工作。它用苍白墨水在活人身上划线，复现自己被划去的命运；墨水落下之处，肢体便失去力量。",
    "A hand of the Roll risen from the enrolling stool, still in the grey livery of the court. It carries the volume it was entered in, and it comes at a caller with the whole weight of the names that volume holds.": "一只从登记凳上站起的名册之手，仍穿着宫廷灰制服。它携带着记有自身名字的卷册，以整卷名字的重量向来访者袭来。"
  });
  Object.assign(globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT, {
    "The Smite": "重击",
    "A trap seen is a trap stripped, and the makings sell at the counter.": "陷阱一经发现便会被拆除，所得材料可在商店出售。",
    "A camp still standing catches the fall, and the long climb is spared.": "只要还有扎好的营地，便能接住这次坠落，省去漫长的上行。",
    "You sleep the deeper for it, and a dream carries the morning twice as far.": "你因此睡得更沉，一个梦让清晨的收获翻了一倍。",
    "the members' rate, then the rope-and-plank crew": "先是成员费率，随后是绳板工队",
    "level 1 unlocks the members' rate; level 2 unlocks the rope-and-plank crew": "等级 1 解锁成员费率；等级 2 解锁绳板工队",
    "+1 choice capacity": "选择队列容量 +1",
    "+1 feat carried upon your papers": "档案可携带专长 +1",
    "your trade's signature working, from degree I to III": "职业招牌法术从 I 阶提升至 III 阶",
    "your trade's signature ability, from level I to III": "职业招牌能力从 I 级提升至 III 级",
    "Random at level 1, then +5 ability points a level": "等级 1 时随机分配，之后每级获得 +5 能力点",
    "Random at level 1, then +5 starting stat points a level": "等级 1 时随机分配，之后每级获得 +5 初始属性点",
    "important letters are kept when the satchel overflows": "信袋溢出时保留重要信件",
    "important choices are protected from queue overflow": "选择队列溢出时保留重要选择",
    "Crit range widened by 1. It stacks with your other crit sources.": "暴击范围扩大 1；可与其他暴击来源叠加。",
    "The Guild counts a nineteen for a twenty upon every check.": "进行任何检定时，行会都将十九点视为二十点。",
    "A 19 counts as a 20 on checks.": "检定中掷出 19 视为 20。",
    "the old rites": "古老仪式",
    "The trophy is one rarity higher.": "战利品稀有度提高一级。",
    "A capstone's toll is 20% lighter.": "终章所需进度降低 20%。",
    "Every kill while it burns feeds it.": "效果燃烧期间，每次击杀都会为其充能。",
    "a wrapping of tomb-linen": "一裹墓葬亚麻布",
    "A keeper of old bargains that has found in the Roll a manifest of debts to her taste. She reckons the terms of the sealed against the living, and she comes in the dark of a rest to press the count. Her tooth she draws for a reckoning, and the reckoning is always against you.": "守护古老契约的夜女巫在名册中发现了一份合她胃口的债务清单。她以封印者的条款清算生者，趁休息时的黑暗前来催收。她拔下一颗牙作为结算凭证，而账目永远对你不利。",
    "The mason set to cut the eighth tomb of the gallery, kept at the work long after the hand that set it. It dresses and squares the stone by the chalked line and the plumb, and it measures every caller against the figure it has yet to fill. Its maul falls where the sword rings off.": "这名石匠奉命开凿长廊的第八座墓穴；下令的手早已消逝，它却仍在劳作。它依粉笔线与铅垂修整方石，并拿每位来客丈量那座尚待填满的墓穴。刀剑弹开的地方，正是它重锤落下之处。",
    "A warden's servant, bound in tomb-linen and laid up in the gallery to keep the tombs it served in life. It rises at a disturbance of the grave-goods and comes on without haste, and the rot of its wrapping carries a curse that stiffens the sinew of the living.": "守门人的仆役，裹着墓葬亚麻布安置在长廊中，死后仍看守生前服侍的墓穴。陪葬品一受惊扰，它便从容起身逼近；腐朽裹布上的诅咒会令生者筋腱僵硬。",
    "A funeral effigy of the gallery, carved crouching with its hands cupped for an offering, that walks when the offering is withheld. It keeps to the tombs it mourns and returns to its post between, and the weight of its stone hands falls as a mason's block falls.": "长廊中的殡葬雕像，刻成蹲伏合掌、等待供品的姿势；供奉一旦中断，它便会行走。它守着所哀悼的墓穴，间歇时回到原位；石手砸落，沉重得如石匠的料石。",
    "A warden of the eldest strata, laid in the gallery under mask and seal, that keeps the count of its tomb though its seal was drawn an age ago. It rises whole, commands the lesser dead of the gallery, and its grave-mask hides a face that death has not been let to finish.": "最古老地层的守门人，戴着面具、覆着封印安葬在长廊中；纵使封印早在久远年代便被揭开，它仍清点着墓中一切。它完整起身，号令长廊里的低阶亡者；墓葬面具下藏着一张不被允许由死亡完成的脸。",
    "A thing of animate chain at home among the great chains of the debtors' deep, where it can scarce be told from the links until the links take hold. It binds and draws its prey to the wall as a debtor is bound to a term, and its barbs are cut to hold and not to loose.": "活化锁链构成的怪物，栖居在债务人深渊的巨链之间；直到链环缠上来之前，几乎分辨不出它的身形。它像条款束缚债务人那样捆住猎物、拖向墙边；链上倒刺只为扣牢而造，从不为松脱。",
    "A debtor of the deep risen from the cell it filed its way out of, still dragging the term it could not serve. It comes on bound in a sprung shackle, and it fights to bind another in its place, that the count of the cells may stand even. What is left of the debtor within is carried along.": "深渊中的债务人从亲手锉开的牢房里复起，仍拖着未能服完的刑期。它戴着崩开的镣铐逼近，竭力把别人锁进自己的位置，好让牢房数目重新对齐。债务人残存的那部分，只能随之而行。",
    "A hyena-headed runner of the counting-house, set down the debtors' gallery to keep the tally of who comes and goes. It counts the living against the manifest by scent, gives tongue at a name it cannot find, and courses in silence at a name it can. Its collar is notched for every quarry it has entered.": "账房派出的鬣狗头信使，驻在债务人长廊，记录所有来去者。它凭气味把生者与清单逐一核对：找不到名字便放声示警，找到名字则无声追猎。项圈上为每个登记过的猎物刻下一道缺口。",
    "A gaoler-fiend of the deep prison, hook-limbed and patient, set to keep the debtors to their cells. It works the gallery on a warder's round, and its sting carries a venom that turns the wound cold and the count against you. It herds before it kills.": "深牢中的狱卒魔，肢体如钩而耐心十足，奉命把债务人关在牢房里。它像狱吏巡更般巡视长廊，尾刺的毒液会令伤口冰冷，也令账目倒向不利于你的一边。它总先驱赶，再下杀手。",
    "The last hand upon the sealing-works, greasing the chains and reading the gauges to the drum's own count. It suffers nothing near the beam and the pumps, and it carries what it fells off to the melt to be poured again, and its rag is black to the elbow.": "封印工场最后的工人，依着转鼓自身的节拍给锁链上油、读取仪表。它不容任何东西靠近横梁与泵机，并把击倒的一切拖去熔炉重新浇铸；手中抹布一直黑到肘部。",
    "A warden of dressed iron built to keep the sealing-works, patient as the beam it stands beside. It moves only when the works are threatened, and then it moves with the whole mass of its make. The floor tells its coming a room ahead through the boots.": "由精整铁料铸成、看守封印工场的守门人，像身旁横梁一样沉着。只有工场受到威胁时它才行动，一动便带着全身铁躯的重量。隔着一间房，脚下地面便会先把它到来的震动传来。",
    "The gathered weeping of the seal, given a shape and a will by an age of being driven back against the wound. It rises from the channels of the works, breaks over a caller in a cold tower, and drags what it takes down the gutters toward the grating. It keeps to the wet.": "封印渗出的泪水汇聚成形；经年累月被逼回裂口，终于生出形体与意志。它从工场沟渠中升起，化作冰冷水塔扑向来客，再把卷走的一切沿排水沟拖向栅栏。它始终依水而行。",
    "A small foul thing of the sealing-works, condensed out of the steam the drum drives back against the wound. It rides the gauge-lines and bursts when it is broken, and the burst carries the heat of the works with it.": "封印工场里污秽的小怪，由转鼓逼回裂口的蒸汽凝结而成。它沿仪表管线游走，破裂时会轰然爆开，并把工场的灼热一并释放。"
  });
  Object.assign(globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT, {
    "A thing chained in the dark an age ago in penance for a debt, and loosed at last when the great chain parted, dragging its own parted iron behind it. It comes on slow and heavy and full of an old grievance, and it fights to fasten its loosed chain upon another and stand free.": "很久以前，这东西因一笔债务被锁在黑暗中赎罪；巨链断裂后，它终于获释，仍拖着自己崩开的铁链。它缓慢而沉重地逼近，满怀陈年怨恨，一心要把松脱的锁链扣到别人身上，好让自己重获自由。",
    "A villager of Hollowmere kept past their dying by the house upon the crag, and sent back down the hill to bar the shutters from the street side. It works by night at the work it did in life, and it answers to its own name.": "空心湖的村民，被峭壁上的宅邸拘留在死亡之后，又遣回山下，从街道一侧闩住百叶窗。它每夜重复生前的劳作，也仍会回应自己的名字。",
    "A brother of Saint Ordel who died with his confession unheard and rose again the same night. It comes upon the living with its hands open, asking the office it was refused, and it treats every refusal as the first.": "圣奥德尔的一名修士，临终忏悔无人聆听，当夜便重新起身。它摊开双手走向生者，请求那场遭到拒绝的仪式；每一次拒绝，在它眼中都如同第一次。",
    "A cold shape among the black reeds with the outline of a woman and the substance of a draught. Its touch takes the warmth out of a limb and leaves it dead to the shoulder, and the reeds close behind it unbent.": "黑色芦苇间的冰冷身影，轮廓像女子，形体却只是一股穿堂寒风。它的触碰会抽走肢体温度，让整条手臂直至肩头失去知觉；它经过后，芦苇原样合拢，一根也不弯折。",
    "A bull-headed giant kept in the undercroft below the gatehouse, whose passages were cut to hold it. It has learned every turn of those cellars, it hunts them by scent, and it keeps at the hunt for as long as the hunt lasts.": "被囚在门楼地下室的牛头巨人，那里的每条通道都是为困住它而开凿。它熟知地窖中的每个转角，凭气味追猎；只要猎物仍在逃，它便永不罢休。",
    "A fiend in the shape of a man with a tiger's head and hands turned backward at the wrist, seated in the Count's own library as a guest of long standing. It was party to the pact that closed the Vale, and it has kept its side of that pact exactly.": "人身虎首、双手从腕部反转的恶魔，以长年宾客的身份坐在伯爵自己的藏书室里。封闭哀悼谷的契约也有它的一份，而它始终分毫不差地履行着自己的条款。",
    "Carry the torch at arm's length from the body, for the stirge strikes at warmth. Take it upon the backswing, as it lifts.": "把火把伸到离身体一臂远处，蚊蝠会扑向热源。趁它拔升时借回挥之势斩下。",
    "The first rush is the whole of its plan. Give ground one pace, let the rush spend itself, and finish the matter upon the turn.": "第一次冲锋便是它全部的谋划。后退一步，让冲势耗尽，再趁它转身时了结。",
    "Carry the pole before you at head height and the snares announce themselves upon it. Choose your footing before you burn a single strand.": "把长杆举到头部高度探在前方，蛛网陷阱自然会挂上去现形。点燃第一根蛛丝前，先选好落脚处。",
    "It fights before an audience, and it treats without one. Bar the gallery door first, and the treating begins at once.": "有观众时它便战斗，无观众时它才谈判。先闩上长廊门，交涉会立刻开始。",
    "Keep the bracers high; the paralysis rides in the claw and enters at the bare forearm. Members who hold Sing Them Down report the stiffness passes the sooner.": "护臂务必抬高；麻痹之力附在利爪上，会从裸露的前臂侵入。掌握“沉歌镇魂”的成员报告说，僵直消退得更快。",
    "Its orders are its whole mind, and the orders name a post. Draw it three paces off the post and its footwork stays behind; gather every rivet, for the rivets are the proof.": "命令就是它全部的心智，而命令指定了一个岗位。把它引离岗位三步，它的步法便会留在原处；每枚铆钉都要收好，那是完成委托的凭证。",
    "Burn the egg-sacs first or fight her twice. The silk takes a fair price cut dry and rolled; folded silk is bought as rag.": "先烧掉卵囊，否则就得与她打上两回。蛛丝晾干成卷后能卖个好价钱；叠起来的只按破布收购。",
    "The heads quarrel over precedence at the first wound, so wound it early and keep the middle distance while they settle it. The settling is the opening.": "一受伤，两颗头便会争论谁该先来；因此尽早伤它，在争执未决时保持中距离。它们解决争端之际，就是你的破绽。",
    "Three heads and one belly, and all three answer when the belly is threatened. Feint low: the goat takes the feint first, and the goat is the honest head.": "三颗头，共用一个肚腹；腹部受威胁时三颗头都会应对。向下佯攻：羊头总是最先上当，而羊头也是三者中最老实的。",
    "In the open dark it is swift past all parrying, so make it come to the lamp, and the lamp evens the account. Tell-Tale Glow marks the fang worth the taking.": "在开阔黑暗中，它快得无从招架；把它引到灯下，灯光便会扳平胜负。“显迹微光”能标出值得取走的那枚獠牙。",
    "Sound the ceiling with the pole before the torch goes under it. A dropped darkmantle smothers the light first, so carry the second candle lit and behind you.": "火把探入前，先用长杆敲探天花板。暗幕怪落下时会先扑灭光源，所以身后还要点着第二支蜡烛。",
    "Walk the corridors pole-first, always: the pole comes back wet, and cheap. What the cube keeps, the cube has priced for you; cut the buckle out from the back face and let the front keep its patience.": "穿行走廊永远让长杆先走：杆子湿着回来，代价也低。立方怪体内留下的东西，等于已经替你标好了价；从背面割出带扣，别去考验正面的耐性。",
    "Count its flock before you touch a single strand, for the shepherd answers the fence-wire faster than the sheep. Fire ruins the silk and the silk is the pay; cut dry, roll tight.": "碰任何一根蛛丝前，先数清它的蛛群；牧者对围栏丝线的反应比群蛛更快。火会毁掉蛛丝，而蛛丝正是报酬；干切，卷紧。",
    "The harpoon comes at the lantern-bearer first, every time, so the lantern rides a pole upon the gunwale. Cut the line before you contest the pull; the tarn wins every tug of war.": "鱼叉每次都会先射向提灯者，所以要把灯挂在舷边的杆上。较力之前先割断绳索；在这片黑湖上，每次拔河都是湖水获胜。",
    "Count the cloaks upon any peg-rail you pass, and count again on the way out. Its moan unmans the unready, so plug one ear with wax and keep the other for your party.": "经过任何挂衣杆时都要数清斗篷，离开时再数一次。它的哀鸣会击溃毫无准备者的心神，所以用蜡塞住一只耳朵，另一只留给队友。",
    "It is the deep's doorbell, and killing it rings it. Shade the lantern to a slit, walk the bed's far edge, and if it cries anyway, stand and meet what comes rather than be met running.": "它是深渊的门铃，杀死它便等于按响铃声。把灯光遮得只剩一线，沿菌床远侧行走；若它终究尖叫，就站稳迎战来者，别在逃跑时被追上。",
    "It stands in the harmless rows on purpose, and the harmless rows lean away from it: read the lean, and prune with the pole-hook at full extension. The frond keeps its virtue dried, and its menace too, so glove the taking.": "它故意混在无害菌丛中，而无害菌丛会向外倾斜躲避。看懂倾向，用完全伸展的长柄钩修剪。叶状体晒干后仍保留药性，也保留危险，采摘时务必戴手套。",
    "Never fight it in its midden, for the ground is its oldest ally. Bait it two rooms upwind with the ration nobody wanted, and mind the third leg: the kick comes from it.": "绝不要在它的垃圾堆里交战，脚下地面是它最老练的盟友。用没人想吃的口粮，在上风方向隔两间房把它引出来；留神第三条腿，踢击正从那里来。",
    "The narrow place with the convenient pillar is the roper, and the pillar's shadow is wrong for the light. Burn the strands at half-reach and keep a knife for the one you missed; the eye closes to fire and to nothing else.": "狭窄处那根位置正好的柱子就是缚索怪，它投下的影子与光线不符。在触须伸到一半时烧断，并留把刀应付漏掉的那根；它的眼睛只会在火焰前闭合。",
    "It fights from the ceiling of its own grief and hurries for nothing. Foul the anchor-lines high on the wall before the first arrow, and it must come down to you, where the drill against spiders serves.": "它倒悬在自身悲苦的顶上作战，从不为任何事匆忙。第一箭射出前，先破坏墙上高处的锚丝，它就不得不落到你面前；到了地面，对付蜘蛛的操练便派得上用场。",
    "Report the flow's width to the member behind you before you do anything else about it. It pours downhill and through gratings, so hold the high ground and spend fire; a blade given to it is a donation.": "采取任何行动前，先把流体宽度报给身后成员。它会沿坡下淌、穿过栅格，所以守住高处并使用火焰；把刀刃砍进它体内，等于白送一件武器。",
    "Touch nothing in the halls with a bare hand until it has been touched with the pole. The tongue-tip is bought dried, and the drying is the seller's own affair.": "厅堂里的任何东西，在长杆碰过之前都不要徒手触摸。商店只收干燥的舌尖，晾晒是卖家自己的事。",
    "The townsfolk below give the hour when asked, and the counterfeit gives it seven minutes early, upon the false bell. Ask, then strike upon the answer.": "下方镇民被问及时都会报出时辰，赝品市民却会依假钟把时间提前七分钟。先问，再按回答出手。",
    "Let it read its warrant entire: the mainspring drives the reading or the truncheon, never both at once. The matter is settled from behind the shoulder while the law is being observed.": "让它把逮捕令从头读完：主发条只能驱动宣读或警棍，无法同时驱动两者。趁它依法办事时，从肩后把事情解决。",
    "It stoops from behind the lamps, so hood the lantern at the cage-rows and listen for the rasp of feather upon brass. A wing-feather in fair condition is bought for the fletchers by the piece.": "它会从灯后俯冲，因此经过笼架时要罩住灯笼，并留心羽毛刮过黄铜的声音。品相完好的翼羽会按根收购，供制箭匠使用。",
    "The breath falls as a fog and settles grey: hold the breath you own, work upwind, and strike behind the foreleg where the plates part. The scales are bought by weight and want no polishing.": "吐息化雾落下，沉积成灰色。屏住自己的呼吸，站在上风处，从前腿后方甲片分开的地方进攻。鳞片按重量收购，无需抛光。",
    "It strikes no body that is reshelving: carry a book, carry it visibly, and put it back wrong. While the warden rights your error, the matter is settled from behind.": "它不会攻击正在把书放回架上的人。带一本书，明明白白拿在手里，再故意放错位置。守架人纠正你的错误时，从背后解决它。",
    "It keeps its circuit to the minute, and the survey has the timetable. Stand aside for its passing and take it at the turn, where the old dismissal was cut to catch it.": "它的巡行分秒不差，勘测记录里已有时刻表。先让到一旁等它经过，再在转角处出手；旧日的驱散法阵正是刻在那里拦截它的。",
    "The blade parts it and buys one breath while it gathers: spend the breath on ground, never on a second stroke. The bead is taken up with a horn spoon and never with the fingers.": "刀刃劈开它后，在其重新聚合前只能换来一息；把这一息用来拉开距离，绝不要浪费在第二刀。水银珠须用角匙舀取，切勿用手指触碰。",
    "Work by the mirrors, for the galleries are hung with them by an arrangement the collection respects. The hair is cut with shears, coiled with the grain, and boxed before it stills.": "借镜面作战；长廊悬镜的布置，是这批藏品也会遵守的规矩。蛇发须用剪刀剪下，顺着纹理盘好，并在彻底静止前装盒。",
    "Warm it and it slows: herd it toward your own lamp and away from the cold air, and take the wing whole once the wax runs soft at the edges.": "加热会让它迟缓：把它赶向自己的灯，远离冷风；等翅翼边缘的蜡软化后，再完整取下。",
    "It follows its last order to the letter, so change what the letter requires: clear the table where you stand and it stands down while you pass. Stitching is cut, never unpicked, and bought by the hand's-length.": "它会一字不差地执行最后一道命令，所以要改变命令所要求的条件：把你身边的桌面清空，它便会停手让你通过。缝线只能割断，不能拆开，并按一掌长收购。",
    "The unfinished side is the safe side: the smooth face keeps no eye and the short arm keeps no grip. Circle to its want of parts and work there.": "未完成的一侧才安全：光滑的半边脸上没有眼睛，短缺的手臂也抓不住东西。绕到它缺少部件的一边，从那里下手。",
    "Hood the lantern and it comes down the stair for a better look, and it comes down within reach. The lens is taken from its collar in a gloved hand. A warm lens is paid double while it still shows the last thing it saw.": "罩住灯笼，它就会下楼凑近观察，也会因此进入攻击距离。要戴手套从颈圈取下镜片；只要温热镜片仍映着它最后所见之物，收购价便翻倍。",
    "It binds what it finds loose among the stacks, so bind nothing of your own to a shelf and keep your hands from the open volumes. Foul its thread at the spool before it works, and it must set the binding to rights before it sets upon you. The thread is bought on the spool, dry.": "它会装订书堆间一切松散之物，所以不要把自己的东西系在书架上，也别把手伸向摊开的书卷。趁它动工前从线轴处弄乱装订线，它就必须先理好线，才会对付你。装订线须保持在线轴上并干燥出售。"
  });
  Object.assign(globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT, {
    "It fights to bind another in its place, so give it no purchase: keep the sprung shackle at pole's length and take the shoulder that drove the door. Break the term it drags and the thrall is a tired debtor again. Members are reminded the debtor was once somebody's line upon the Roll.": "它想把别人锁进自己的位置，绝不能让它抓牢：用长杆把崩开的镣铐挡在远处，攻击撞开牢门的那侧肩膀。打断它拖着的刑期，债奴就会重新变成一个疲惫的债务人。提醒各位成员：这个债务人也曾是名册上的某一行姓名。",
    "It wakes only to a threat against the works, so threaten the works and take it as it turns: spike a gauge, and it must attend the needle first, the machinery outranking the caller in its orders. Iron cast so heavy turns the point, so meet it with the flat and the head. The ingot is bought as scrap of a good grade.": "它只会因工场受到威胁而苏醒，所以就威胁工场，趁它转身时出手：卡住一只仪表，它必须先处理指针，因为在命令中，机械的优先级高于来客。如此厚重的铸铁会弹开刃尖，应用剑身平面与锤头应对。铁锭按优质废铁收购。",
    "It bursts when it is broken, so break it at the length of a polearm and turn your face from it. Bleed a gauge-line and it goes to the leak before it goes to you. The scalded glass is bought whole and is worth nothing cracked.": "它破裂时会爆炸，所以要隔着长柄武器的距离击破，并把脸转开。给仪表管线放气，它会先奔向泄漏处而不是你。烫蚀玻璃只收完整品，裂开便一文不值。",
    "The coil sears through mail, so give it no coil: keep it at the sword's length and off the laid hearth, where its heat is least. Herd it from the mantel, for it fights hardest to keep the jar. Draw the ember-scale with tongs and bed it in sand until it will bear a hand.": "它的盘绕足以灼穿锁甲，所以别让它缠上：保持一剑之距，把它赶离铺好的炉床，那里的热量最低。把它从壁炉架旁逼走；为了守住罐子时，它反抗得最凶。余烬鳞片须用火钳拔取，埋进沙中，直到能用手承托。",
    "It fights to keep the seventh seal from the striking, so make for the seventh: threaten the whole seal and it must stand before it rather than before you. The signet-die is heavy and slow, so take it on the turn. The die is drawn cold and entered under seal, the impression not to be taken.": "它为保护第七封印不被敲击而战，所以直奔第七道：威胁整个封印，它就必须挡在封印前，而不是挡在你面前。印玺模具沉重迟缓，趁它转身时出手。模具须冷却后取出，密封登记，严禁拓印。",
    "It fills the gallery wall to wall, so take the high ground of a stair or a sill and keep it in front of you. Steel comes back pitted from it. The rind is dried and glazed before it will keep.": "它从一面墙填满到另一面墙，所以占据阶梯或门槛的高处，让它始终留在正前方。钢铁接触后会布满蚀坑。外皮必须干燥上釉，才能保存。",
    "Keep moving along the wall it cuts and take it as it stoops to the line, for it is slow to leave a course half-dressed. Its reach is longer than its arms look, cut for work above its own head, so chalk your distance and add a pace. The inverted chisel is drawn from the drowned hand.": "沿着它正在凿削的墙不断移动，趁它俯身对准线条时攻击；它不愿离开只修整了一半的墙层。它的有效距离比手臂看起来更长，那双臂本就为头顶作业而造，所以用粉笔标出距离后还要再加一步。倒置凿子要从溺亡之手中拔出。",
    "It fights slow and defends the one course, so draw it off the wall it is cutting and its patience has nothing to keep. The mallet falls heavy and true but seldom, so spend the wait and strike between. The mallet is bought as drowned iron, less the water.": "它行动缓慢，只守着正在砌的那一层墙。把它引离墙面，它的耐心便无处安放。木槌落下又重又准，却并不频繁；利用等待的空档，在两击之间进攻。木槌按溺水铁器收购，水重不计。",
    "Never let its cold hand settle, for a hand laid on is a record lifted: keep it at the pole's length and take it before it closes. Members carry a fair copy of their own papers sealed against the skin, that what it lifts may be entered again above. The blank margin is bought by the shred, dry.": "绝不要让它冰冷的手落稳；一旦按住，便会抄走一份记录。用长杆保持距离，在它合拢手掌前击倒。成员须贴身密封携带自己档案的誊本，以便被它抄走的内容能在上方重新登记。空白页边按干燥碎片收购。",
    "It works upon what is written, so carry nothing written that you mean to keep, and set a blank leaf in its way instead. It stops to keep the blank leaf. The signature is bought uncut.": "它只对有字之物下手，所以不要携带任何想保住的文字，改在路上放一张白纸。它会停下来保管那张白纸。签名须完整未裁才予收购。",
    "It is small and far stronger than its size, so do not close and grapple, but keep it at the pole and break the parted links it runs upon. It fastens as a fetter fastens, so cut the hold before it sets. The parted fetter is bought by the length, cold.": "它体形虽小，力量却远超尺寸；不要贴身擒抱，要用长杆拉开距离，击碎它奔行其上的断裂链环。它会像镣铐一样扣死，所以务必在锁紧前斩断抓握。断裂镣铐冷却后按长度收购。",
    "It bides at its anchor and reaches the length of its bond, so mark the anchors as you pass and keep beyond the reach of each. Cut the parted bond, not the thing, for the bond is where its strength runs. An anchorite's parted link is drawn cold and paid by the piece.": "它守在锚点旁，攻击范围就是锁链长度；经过时标出每处锚点，并始终留在其触及范围之外。要斩断已经分裂的束缚，而非攻击本体，因为力量正沿束缚流动。锚居者的断链须冷却取下，按件计价。",
    "It runs the links faster than a horse and swallows whole, so give it no straight gallery to charge: fight it at a turn or an anchor, where its length works against it. Hold your breath through the first crack of its lightning-breath. The storm-scale is drawn cold and carried in oil, for the oil keeps the charge off the hand that bears it.": "它沿链环奔行，比马还快，也会把猎物整个吞下；不要给它可供冲锋的笔直长廊，应在转角或锚点处交战，让细长身躯反成累赘。第一声雷电吐息炸响时要屏住呼吸。风暴鳞片须冷却取下，浸油携带，以免电荷传到持有者手上。",
    "It draws across you like a mark tallied, in sevens, so count with it: six strokes, and the seventh is its whole strength, and the seventh is your opening. Break the eye-line at the first stroke. The tally-scratch is a rubbing, taken dry and paid to the survey.": "它像计数刻痕般掠过你，以七为一组；跟着它数：前六击之后，第七击会倾尽全力，也正是你的破绽。第一击时便切断视线。计数划痕以干拓本采集，由勘测处支付报酬。",
    "It comes on slow and certain, so give ground and keep the middle distance and let the count spend itself upon your retreat. Break its eye from the tally at the first stroke. The counting-bead is drawn from the wire whole.": "它缓慢却坚定地逼近；后退并保持中距离，让它的计数耗费在追赶上。第一击时便切断它与计数之间的视线。计数珠须从金属线上完整取下。",
    "It fights to keep the last count uncalled, so call it: press it toward the thing beneath, and it must stand between you and the count rather than come on. It is vast and slow, so keep the middle distance and spend the gaps. The final token is drawn from the fallen debt and entered under seal, the last such the Roll will take.": "它为阻止最后一笔账被宣读而战，那就把账念出来：把它逼向下方之物，它便不得不挡在你和账目之间，无法继续进攻。它庞大而迟缓，保持中距离，利用每个空档。最终信物从倒下的债务中取出，密封登记；这是名册会收下的最后一件。",
    "The plated back turns most blows; take it underneath, where the shale gives way to soft hide, and let the tremor pass before you close. A scute prised from the living plate is bought at a good price.": "甲片覆盖的背部能弹开大多数攻击；从下方出手，那里页岩让位于柔软皮肉。震动过去后再靠近。从活甲上撬下的鳞甲能卖个好价钱。",
    "It strikes at the light and at the face, so set the lantern down at arm's length and fight beside it rather than behind it. The rasped tongue wants drying before it is packed, or it sours in a day.": "它会攻击光源与人的脸，所以把灯笼放在一臂之外，在灯旁作战，不要躲在灯后。磨粗的舌头装包前必须晾干，否则一天便会腐败。",
    "It goes for the pack before the man, so let the pack fall and take it while it stoops. The peat-black pelt is bought cured, and a torn one is bought at nothing.": "它先扑背包，再扑人；丢下背包，趁它俯身时出手。泥炭般漆黑的毛皮只收鞣制完好的，撕破便一文不值。",
    "Stand still and it comes to you, which is the only ground of your choosing you will get. It goes out at the first heavy blow, so lead with the heaviest you carry.": "站着不动，它自然会来找你；这是唯一能由你选择的战场。第一次重击便能让它熄灭，所以起手就用最沉的家伙。",
    "Call it by its name off the doorpost and it stops for a breath, and a breath is enough. The shutter-bar is oak and heavy and worth carrying only in a light pack.": "照门柱上的名字呼唤它，它会停顿一息，而一息已经足够。百叶窗横闩是沉重橡木，只有背包轻时才值得带走。",
    "Silver, or the wound closes while you watch. It runs for the drains at half its strength, so put a body on the grate before you close.": "必须用银，否则伤口会在眼前愈合。体力降到一半时它会逃向排水道，因此靠近前先派人守住栅口。",
    "Take the bell-rope out of his hand first and the whole office falls apart, for he cannot call the rest without it. The frayed end is bought by the fathom.": "先从他手中夺走钟绳，整套仪式便会瓦解；没有钟绳，他无法召来其余亡者。磨损的绳端按英寻收购。",
    "The chain is still upon it and fouls at a corner, so fight it where the lane turns and not in the open. The kennel collar is bought as evidence, not as leather.": "锁链仍拴在它身上，经过转角便会缠住；应在巷道拐弯处交战，不要选开阔地。犬舍项圈按证物而非皮革收购。",
    "They stand among the true thorn and are known by the root-knot they walk on, so watch the ground rather than the branch. Dry twig burns, and a stand of them clears in one draw of flame.": "它们混在真正的荆棘中，靠用于行走的根瘤才能辨认；所以要看地面，不要看枝条。枯枝易燃，一道火焰便能清掉一整丛。",
    "They loose together, so never cross a ride in the open where two stands can see you. The sheaf of needles is bought by the apothecary and must be carried in a stiff case.": "它们会齐射，所以绝不要在两丛灌木都能看见你的开阔林道上穿行。针刺成束卖给药剂师，必须装在硬盒里携带。",
    "Bargain if you must and hold her to the letter, for she holds you to yours. Fighting her in her own water is the worst ground in the Vale; draw her onto the ride.": "若非谈不可，就逐字约束她，因为她也会逐字约束你。在她自己的水域作战，是哀悼谷最糟的地形；把她引上林道。",
    "It walks the rows and will not leave them, so break off across the ditch and it lets you go. Take it at the joint where the harness binds. The horn is bought whole and is worth nothing split.": "它沿成排墓穴行走，绝不离开；跨过沟渠脱身，它便会放弃追击。攻击挽具勒住的关节。完整的角才会被收购，裂开便一文不值。",
    "It works the rows in their numbered order, so stand in a row it has already cut and it passes you by. The rusted hook is bought as abbey work and wants no cleaning.": "它依编号顺序修剪各排树木，所以站进已经修过的一排，它便会从你身边经过。锈钩作为修道院遗物收购，无需清理。",
    "They quarrel over the dig, so wait for the quarrel and take them apart in it. They will not follow past the wall. The scavenged jawbone is bought by the piece.": "它们会为挖掘物争吵，等争执开始，再趁机逐个解决。它们不会追过围墙。拾来的颚骨按件收购。",
    "Never take the guide it offers, and if you have taken it, leave the reeds by the way you came. Its jaw is bought as proof that the guide was refused.": "绝不要接受它带路；若已经接受，就沿原路离开芦苇荡。它的颚骨会被当作拒绝向导的凭证收购。",
    "It reaches for a hand, so give it a blade and keep the hand. The sodden ribbon dries out white and is bought by the ell.": "它会伸手来牵，那就递给它刀刃，保住自己的手。湿透的丝带晾干后会变白，按厄尔收购。",
    "Its touch kills a limb to the shoulder, so fight it at length or not at all. A bundle of black reed keeps its cold for a day and is packed away from food.": "它一碰便能让整条肢体直至肩头失去知觉，所以要么远距离交战，要么别打。一束黑芦苇的寒意可维持一天，打包时须远离食物。",
    "Fire is no use and lightning is worse, for both feed it; cut it apart and scatter the parts. Fen-thatch is bought by weight and comes up light once dried.": "火焰毫无用处，雷电更糟，两者都会滋养它；把它切碎，再将各部分分散。沼泽茅草按重量收购，干燥后会轻得多。",
    "It hunts the cellars by scent, so leave the pack at the stair and go down light. The broken horn is bought by the pair, and only one is ever taken.": "它凭气味在地窖里追猎，所以把背包留在楼梯口，轻装下去。断角按一对收购，可每次永远只能取到一只。",
    "It walks the same road every time, so learn the road and be somewhere else upon it. The cut canvas is bought as house goods and is priced by the face upon it.": "它每次都走同一条路线，记住路线，再站到它不会经过的位置。割下的画布按宅邸物品收购，价格取决于画上是谁的脸。",
    "It wears the face the sleeper trusts, so set the watch in pairs and let no one keep it alone. The token taken from a sleeper is bought sealed and is never handled twice.": "它会戴上沉睡者信任的面孔，所以守夜必须两人一组，绝不让任何人独自值守。从沉睡者身上取下的信物须密封出售，任何人都不可触碰第二次。",
    "Common steel does nothing at all to it; bring a blessed edge up the crag or leave it in its chair. The backward palm is bought at the library's own price, and the library asks no questions.": "普通钢铁完全伤不了它；要么把受祝福的刀刃带上峭壁，要么任它坐在椅中。反掌按藏书室自定的价格收购，藏书室不会多问。"
  });
  Object.assign(globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT, {
    "the remnant the settling left behind, that walks among the salvage-gangs and the recovery-lamps and troubles no one that keeps to the light": "沉降后留下的残影，游荡在打捞队与搜救灯之间；只要守着光，便不会受它侵扰",
    "You choose the fire. When the Count is down you will lay him in his own hearth with the beams of his own roof upon him, and burn the hall about him until there is nothing in it to rise. The answer is entered upon the Roll.": "你选择火焰。伯爵倒下后，你会把他放进他自己的大壁炉，让自家屋梁压在身上，再焚尽整座厅堂，直到里面再无任何东西能够起身。这个答案已记入名册。",
    "Corvane goes down at the chapel door, and you lay him in the great hearth he has kept swept three hundred years, and pull the roof-beams in upon him, and set the whole hall alight.": "科尔瓦恩倒在礼拜堂门前。你把他放进那座由他清扫了三百年的大壁炉，拉下屋梁压住他，点燃整座厅堂。",
    "You choose the morning. When the Count is down you will carry the reliquary of Saint Ordel through the chapel door he wedged shut, set it upon the altar where it belongs, and take the shutters off the whole east front. The answer is entered upon the Roll.": "你选择清晨。伯爵倒下后，你会把圣奥德尔的圣物匣带过那扇被他顶死的礼拜堂门，安放在本应属于它的祭坛上，再拆下东面全部百叶窗。这个答案已记入名册。",
    "Corvane goes down against the chapel door, and you draw the beam out of it, and carry the reliquary of Saint Ordel in and set it upon the altar it was cut for, and pull the shutters off the east front one after another.": "科尔瓦恩倒在礼拜堂门上。你抽出顶门的横梁，把圣奥德尔的圣物匣带进去，放上为它凿成的祭坛，再逐一拆下东面的百叶窗。",
    "You choose the seat. When the Count is down you will take the signet off his hand, sit at the head of his own table, and keep the Vale as he kept it, which is the only way anyone has ever found to keep it. The answer is entered upon the Roll.": "你选择席位。伯爵倒下后，你会从他手上取下印戒，坐上他自己长桌的首席，像他一样守住这座山谷——这是世人发现的唯一守谷之法。这个答案已记入名册。",
    "You choose the name. The register out of Saint Ordel carries the whole of it in the abbey's own hand, written before ever there was a count in this valley, and when he is down you will read it out over him and let the pact answer to it. The answer is entered upon the Roll.": "你选择名字。圣奥德尔的登记簿以修道院亲笔记着那个完整姓名，写成之时，这座山谷甚至还没有伯爵。他倒下后，你会在他身前把名字高声读出，让契约自行回应。这个答案已记入名册。",
    "Corvane goes down at the chapel door, and you open the abbey register at the page and read out the name he was christened, Aurel, in the abbey's own hand and before ever there was a count in this valley, and the whole pact turns over to hear it.": "科尔瓦恩倒在礼拜堂门前。你翻开修道院登记簿的那一页，读出他受洗时得到的名字——奥雷尔。那是修道院的亲笔，写于这座山谷尚无伯爵之时；整个契约都翻转过来聆听。",
    "He went down with the Pellinger party in the spring and carried their lamp for eleven days after the last of them stopped walking.": "他在春天随佩林杰小队下行；队中最后一人停止行走后，他又替他们提了十一天的灯。",
    "She followed her husband's company down and outlived every one of them on what she could pick off the walls.": "她跟随丈夫的队伍下行，只靠从墙上摘取的东西活命，最终比队中每个人都活得更久。",
    "Won off a mimic put down by the free stroke, the tooth in the hinge seen while the lid is still up, so the thing never has a move of its own, and no other way.": "取自一只被自由一击放倒的宝箱怪：趁箱盖尚未落下便看见铰链里的牙，让它从未得到自己的行动机会。除此之外别无取得方法。",
    "It eats the strokes that came apart, off the thorn where it hangs them, and it grows on your best work.": "它吃掉挂在荆棘上那些溃散的攻击，并以你最出色的战果成长。",
    "It goes under the bad ground instead of over it and comes up on the far side, and it has the level road by heart.": "它不从险地上方经过，而会钻入地下，从另一端出来；平坦道路的每一寸都刻在它心里。",
    "It is on the stair before you have decided to take the stair, and the road behind it comes out shorter than the road was.": "你尚未决定是否踏上阶梯，它已经到了阶梯上；跟在它身后，道路总比原先更短。",
    "it is upon you before your feet are under you, and your own stroke waits": "你尚未站稳，它已扑到身前，而你自己的攻击仍在等待",
    "Recovered whole. The armourer's report reads: maker unknown, edge unaccountable, scabbard to be issued at the bearer's own risk.": "完整回收。军械师报告写道：制作者不明，锋刃无法解释；剑鞘可予发放，持有者须自行承担风险。",
    "Dried leaf by leaf at the Library's expense. Three pages remain shut fast to one another, and the copyists have stopped prying.": "由藏书室出资逐页烘干。仍有三页紧紧粘合，抄写员已停止撬动。",
    "Catalogued as ornament, by order. The night-porter has asked that it face the wall, and the request is granted in the minutes.": "奉命以装饰品编目。夜班门房请求将其面朝墙壁，会议记录已批准这项请求。",
    "Dwarf-make, sound, and cut for no vault the survey names. Filed under patience.": "矮人工艺，完好无损；齿形不对应勘测记录中的任何宝库。归档于“耐心”等待。",
    "Recovered sealed; opened once, by the clerk of that year; resealed the same afternoon, by the same clerk, at his own request.": "回收时处于密封状态；当年的书记员曾开启一次，同日下午又由同一名书记员应本人要求重新封印。",
    "A fair copy, correct to the comma, of a page the bearer had yet to write when it was found. The library keeps it face down, under glass, and asks that the glass be left alone.": "一份工整誊本，连逗号都分毫不差；发现它时，持有者还没有写下原页。藏书室将其正面朝下压在玻璃下，并要求任何人不要触碰玻璃。",
    "It writes in any hand it has once seen, and it is entered in the inventory as dry, to be kept so. The inventory is checked weekly.": "它能模仿见过的任何笔迹。库存簿将其登记为“无墨”，并要求始终如此保存。库存每周检查一次。",
    "Warm at recovery and paid double, per the posted rate. It has shown nothing since, and the night-porter stores it facing the wall regardless.": "回收时尚有余温，依公示费率支付双倍报酬。此后它再未显示任何景象，夜班门房仍坚持将其朝墙存放。",
    "The ribbon that ruled his page. The library measured it three times and got three lengths, and files the mean, under the measurer's written protest.": "曾为他的纸页划出格线的缎带。藏书室量了三次，得到三种长度，只得在测量员书面抗议的附注下，将平均值归档。",
    "Orders for castings run back an age, each marked settled in strong chalk. The last order stands open, and the works that would have filled it stand cold.": "浇铸订单可追溯到久远年代，每一份都以粗重粉笔标记结清。最后一份仍未完成，而本应完成它的工场已经冰冷。",
    "Ground crystal in a brass frame, found folded upon the eyepiece. The library entered them as plain glass, then amended the entry, then locked the drawer.": "打磨水晶配黄铜镜架，发现时折放在目镜上。藏书室先登记为普通玻璃，随后修订条目，最后锁上抽屉。",
    "Drawn from a tomb-lamp still burning after an age underground. Decanted, sealed and shelved; the sample burns yet in its phial, and the library keeps a wet cloth beside it as a rule.": "取自一盏在地下燃烧了漫长岁月仍未熄灭的墓灯。灯油经分装、密封后上架；样品至今仍在小瓶中燃烧，藏书室按规定在旁边常备湿布。",
    "A surveyor's lodestone, lost on some earlier descent and recovered far below where it was dropped. It points down, and holds to it however the case is turned.": "勘测员的天然磁石，早先某次下行时遗失，却在坠落地点远下方寻回。它始终指向下方，无论怎样转动外盒都不改变方向。",
    "Silver-gilt and sound, seal whole, drawn up out of Ysmere on a drag-line after three hundred years in water that gives nothing back. The chapel of Castle Corvane was raised around this box, and the box was in the lake, and the chapel was shuttered from within.": "鎏银外壳完好，封印完整；在一片从不归还任何东西的水域中沉了三百年后，以拖绳从伊斯梅尔打捞而出。科尔瓦恩城堡的礼拜堂原是围绕这只匣子建造，可匣子一直在湖中，而礼拜堂的百叶窗却从内部闩死。",
    "The rain keeps the vermin to their holes: a quarter fewer ambushes while it falls.": "雨水把害兽困在巢穴里：降雨期间伏击减少四分之一。",
    "The murk stands against the watch: 2 off the eye that looks for traps and for ambushes.": "昏暗雾气妨碍警戒：发现陷阱与伏击的侦察 -2。",
    "The cold drives the beasts deep: half as many ambushes while it holds.": "严寒把野兽赶入深处：寒霜持续期间伏击减半。",
    "Every sound carries in the dead air: 2 upon the watch against traps and ambushes.": "死寂空气会传递每一道声响：发现陷阱与伏击的侦察 +2。",
    "The draught worries the lantern: 1 off the watch against traps and ambushes.": "上涌气流扰动灯火：发现陷阱与伏击的侦察 -1。",
    "The water shuts the low ways, and the roads it forces are often the shorter: shortcuts come up half again as often.": "上涨水位封住低处道路，被迫改走的路线往往更短：捷径出现率提高一半。",
    "Nothing moves and nothing sounds, so what does is heard at once: 2 upon the watch against traps and ambushes.": "万物不动，万籁无声，因此任何动静都会立即被听见：发现陷阱与伏击的侦察 +2。",
    "The current carries the deep's leavings past, and some are worth the taking: chests come up half again as often.": "冷流把深渊遗落之物带到身旁，其中有些值得拾取：宝箱出现率提高一半。",
    "The shaking springs the old works before you reach them: a third fewer traps left set.": "震动会在你抵达前触发古老机关：仍处于布设状态的陷阱减少三分之一。",
    "The frost takes the lantern-glass: 2 off the watch against traps and ambushes.": "寒霜蒙住灯罩玻璃：发现陷阱与伏击的侦察 -2。",
    "The mist gives fifty paces and keeps the rest: half again as many ambushes.": "浓雾只肯让出五十步视野，其余尽数藏起：伏击增加一半。",
    "The frost puts everything living to ground: half as many ambushes while it holds.": "致命寒霜让一切活物伏地不出：寒霜持续期间伏击减半。",
    "All that walks below is risen, and the old rites answer over every carcass.": "下方行走的一切都已复起，古老仪式会回应每具躯壳。"
  });
  Object.assign(globalThis.LOWMOOR_ZH_EXACT, {
    "1 point. One of three, and it may be changed later for nothing. Opens with any major skill in this quarter.": "消耗 1 点。三选一，之后可免费更改。本分区任一主要技能均可将其解锁。",
    "The wall at Mereward has stood bare a while, and nobody had gone through the last pack. In it is a gauntlet with a hand still in it, and the hand closes on yours when you take it:": "梅里沃德的墙已经空置了一阵子，上一批遗物始终无人挑选。其中有一只仍装着手掌的护手；你将它拿起时，那只手握住了你的手：",
    "A chest stands against the wall with its lid a finger open, and there is a tooth in the hinge. <b>You open on it first.</b>": "一只箱子靠墙立着，箱盖张开一指宽，铰链里露出一颗牙。<b>你抢先向它出手。</b>",
    "A chest stands against the wall with its lid a finger open, and as your hand goes to it the lid comes down. <b>It was never a chest.</b>": "一只箱子靠墙立着，箱盖张开一指宽；你的手刚伸过去，箱盖便猛然落下。<b>它从来就不是箱子。</b>",
    "There is a second stair here that no chart records, and it comes out upon the landing the first one left you at. You enter it for the survey and go on.": "这里还有第二道阶梯，任何图表都未曾记录；它最终通向第一道阶梯带你离开的那处平台。你把它记入勘测记录，继续前行。",
    "Terms Pending": "条款待定",
    "The draconic rolls are kept by subscription, and this one's subscription went unpaid.": "龙族名册采用订阅制，而这一位没有续费。",
    "Wisdom is the watch itself: the trap, the ambush and the false chest are seen before they are sprung.": "感知就是警戒本身：陷阱、伏击和假宝箱都会在发动前被发现。",
    "The account closes with a sword hung upon the mess-room wall, edge out above the hearth.": "账目以一柄挂在食堂墙上的剑作结；剑刃朝外，悬在壁炉上方。",
    "The account closes upon a chart signed in the corner, the road drawn plain for the next hand down.": "账目以一张角落签名的图表作结；下行道路清楚绘出，留给下一位接手者。",
    "The account closes upon an oath sworn open, filed among the living against a return.": "账目以一份公开立下的誓言作结；誓言归入生者档案，以防其归来。",
    "The account closes in the quartermaster's column: one torch burned to the collar, the tag come home with its bearer.": "账目在军需官的栏中作结：一支烧到套环的火把，一块随持有者归来的名牌。",
    "Vhorren's hoard is yours to pick over, and one thing in it was never coin.": "沃伦的宝藏任你翻检，其中有一样东西从来就不是钱币。",
    "You set the lock with the flat of your sword-arm, driving the lead home as a soldier drives a picket.": "你用持剑手臂的平面压紧锁扣，像士兵把桩打入地面一样将铅块楔到底。",
    "Every upgrade is unbought and every prestige point returns to the purse, exactly as it was paid. Titles are earned, not bought, and stand. An upgrade already enjoyed at this enrolment keeps its effect for the chronicle in hand.": "所有升级都会取消购买，每一点声望都按原价退回钱袋。称号靠功绩赢得，并非购买所得，因此会保留。本次登记时已经享受过的升级，其效果会继续作用于当前编年史。",
    "The muster is off the board. Your hours at it stand in your record of musters, with the badges they took.": "本次集结已从公告板撤下。你参与的时数仍保存在集结记录中，所得徽章也会一并保留。",
    "Your voice needs a badge behind it, and the first comes at one hour stood here.": "你的发言需要徽章作为凭据；在此值守满 1 小时即可获得第一枚。",
    "The Standing Order: the house hires a licensed feat onto an empty set of papers, while the purse holds three times the price.": "常设命令：钱袋余额达到价格三倍时，行会大厅会把一项已解锁专长自动雇用到空白档案中。",
    "The little window is refused by the browser. Allow pop-ups for this page and ask again, or fold to the strip instead.": "浏览器拒绝打开小窗口。请允许此页面弹出窗口后重试，或改为折叠成窄条。",
    "You make camp. The torch is banked and the watch set, and the descent holds until you break camp.": "你扎下营地，封存火把，安排守夜；在你拔营前，下行会停在此处。",
    "The code is written out to a file. Look for it among your downloads.": "代码已写入文件，请在下载目录中查找。",
    "[S] EMBER SHOPPE": "[S] 余烬商店"
  });
})();

