    "The ink runs into every seam of the harness and dries there, and the joints answer stiffly.": "墨水流进挽具每道接缝，在里面干结，关节动作也随之僵硬。",
    "It takes the fee it has always taken, in plate, off whoever comes down the aisle.": "无论谁沿过道下行，它都会照旧收取费用，而支付之物正是身上的甲片。",
    "The barrow-cold goes in at the wrist and settles somewhere behind the ribs.": "古墓寒意从手腕钻入，最后沉在肋骨后方某处。",
